-- impairment-non-financial-assets-psak-236: content_json backfill (the document content was serialised from)
with up as (
  update public.essays e
     set content_json = $j${"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"In brief"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"An asset may not be carried at more than the entity can get back from it. PSAK 236 checks this in three steps. The entity looks for indications at every reporting date, estimates the "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"recoverable amount"},{"type":"text","text":" (the higher of fair value less costs of disposal and value in use) when there is one, and writes the asset down to that amount if it is below the carrying amount."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Most long-lived assets do not earn cash on their own, so the test usually runs on a "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"cash-generating unit"},{"type":"text","text":" (CGU). A CGU's loss goes first to its goodwill and then pro rata to its other assets, and no asset is pushed below its own recoverable amount or zero."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"An impairment loss on any asset except goodwill is reversed when the estimates behind recoverable amount improve, but only up to the carrying amount the asset would have had with no impairment. The passage of time alone is not a reason to reverse."}]}]}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PT Pertamina Hulu Energi and subsidiaries (PHE) report a provision for impairment of non-financial assets of 215,666 for 2024 against 707,087 for 2023, in USD thousand, on a line of its own below gross profit (PHE FS 2024, statement of profit or loss, Daftar 2/1, PDF p. 14; \"Daftar\" is the printed page). The charge is 1.5 percent of revenue and 4.3 percent of gross profit in 2024, against 4.9 and 12.5 percent in 2023."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"After reading this page a student should be able to decide when an asset must be tested, compute a recoverable amount, allocate a CGU's loss and its reversal, and record each step in journals."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"All amounts are in USD thousand unless stated. Figures from PHE's statements are cited to their note. Every other number is labelled an illustration."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. What impairment is and which assets PSAK 236 covers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Depreciation spreads an asset's cost over its life without asking whether that cost will come back. Impairment asks. PSAK 236 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Penurunan Nilai Aset"},{"type":"text","text":" (formerly PSAK 48, IAS 36) requires that an asset be carried at no more than its recoverable amount, the amount to be recovered through use or sale (para. 1). An "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"impairment loss"},{"type":"text","text":" is the excess of carrying amount over recoverable amount (para. 6)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard covers what other standards leave out (para. 2). Inventories follow the lower of cost and NRV in PSAK 202, financial assets the expected credit loss model of PSAK 109, and deferred tax, employee benefit and contract assets, investment property at fair value, biological assets at fair value less costs to sell and assets held for sale their own standards. What remains is the core of a balance sheet: fixed assets, oil and gas properties, right-of-use assets, intangibles, goodwill, and investments in subsidiaries, associates and joint ventures (para. 4)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"US GAAP tests in two steps. A "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"recoverability test"},{"type":"text","text":" first compares carrying amount with the undiscounted cash flows the asset will produce; only if it fails is the asset written down to fair value. IFRS goes straight to a discounted measure. For example (illustration), a production facility carried at 500,000 is expected to produce undiscounted net cash flows of 560,000. A buyer would pay 430,000 net of costs, and the present value of its cash flows is 450,000."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"US GAAP (two steps)"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 236 (one step)"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Test"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Undiscounted cash flows 560,000 > carrying amount 500,000: passes"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Recoverable amount = higher of 430,000 and 450,000 = 450,000"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Loss"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"none"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"500,000 − 450,000 = 50,000"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The undiscounted test ignores the time value of money, so an asset whose cash arrives slowly passes it while worth less than its carrying amount. PSAK 236 catches that asset earlier and, as section 8 shows, lets the loss come back if conditions improve; US GAAP forbids reversal for assets held and used."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2. When an asset must be tested"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"At the end of each reporting period the entity assesses whether there is any "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"indication"},{"type":"text","text":" of impairment, and only if there is does it estimate recoverable amount (para. 9)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The minimum list of indications has two halves (para. 12)."}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"External"},{"type":"text","text":": a market value that has fallen more than time and use explain; adverse changes in the technological, market, economic or legal environment; higher market interest rates that raise the discount rate and lower recoverable amount materially; net assets above market capitalisation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Internal"},{"type":"text","text":": obsolescence or physical damage; an asset becoming idle, a plan to discontinue or restructure, a plan to dispose of it early; internal reports showing performance worse than expected, such as cash needs above budget or actual cash flows below it (para. 14)."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Upstream, the usual triggers are price, discount rate, reserves and delays (section 11). Materiality applies. If earlier calculations showed recoverable amount well above carrying amount and nothing has happened to close the gap, no new estimate is needed (para. 15). An indication that leads to no loss may still call for a shorter useful life or a different depreciation method (para. 17)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Goodwill, intangibles with indefinite lives and intangibles not yet available for use are tested every year whether or not there is an indication (para. 10). PHE's policy follows the same split (Note 3w, Daftar 5/72, PDF p. 89)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3. Recoverable amount and fair value less costs of disposal"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Recoverable amount is the higher of "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"fair value less costs of disposal"},{"type":"text","text":" (FVLCD) and "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"value in use"},{"type":"text","text":" (VIU) (para. 18). A rational owner either sells the asset or keeps using it, whichever is worth more, so the asset is impaired only if both routes fall short. If either measure exceeds the carrying amount, the other need not be computed (para. 19)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Fair value"},{"type":"text","text":" is the exit price between market participants under PSAK 113 (formerly PSAK 68, IFRS 13). "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Costs of disposal"},{"type":"text","text":" are the incremental costs of selling, such as legal costs, transfer taxes and the cost of removing the asset; termination benefits and the cost of reorganising what remains are not (para. 28). Once an asset meets the held-for-sale criteria it leaves PSAK 236 for PSAK 105 (formerly PSAK 58, IFRS 5)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), take as the starting point PHE's East Kalimantan and Attaka block, carried at 369,670 and written down in 2024 to an estimated recoverable amount of 305,466 (Note 17). Suppose a buyer had offered 330,000 for the participating interest, with 2,000 of legal costs and 3,000 of transfer charges."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"FVLCD = 330,000 − 2,000 − 3,000 = 325,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Recoverable amount = higher of 325,000 and 305,466 = 325,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Impairment loss = 369,670 − 325,000 = 44,670, against 369,670 − 305,466 = 64,204 if, as PHE's figure implies, nothing above 305,466 were available"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 19,534 difference is why the standard asks which basis was used (para. 130(e))."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4. Value in use"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"VIU is the present value of the cash flows the entity expects from the asset (para. 6). It is entity-specific, so unlike fair value it may reflect synergies and rights only the current owner has (para. 53A). The standard builds it from five elements: expected cash flows, possible variations in their amount and timing, the time value of money, the price of bearing uncertainty, and other factors such as illiquidity (para. 30). Uncertainty may be reflected either in the cash flows or in the rate, but not in both (para. 32)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Cash flow rules."},{"type":"text","text":" Four rules shape the projections."}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Projections rest on reasonable and supportable assumptions, with greater weight on external evidence, and on approved budgets for at most five years unless a longer period can be justified (para. 33)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cash flows are for the asset "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"in its current condition"},{"type":"text","text":". Inflows from a restructuring the entity is not committed to, or from spending that would enhance the asset, are left out (para. 44), while spending to maintain its current performance is included (para. 49)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Financing flows and income tax are left out (para. 50), because the rate already prices money and is set before tax. Cash flows of recognised liabilities, such as a decommissioning provision, are left out to avoid counting them twice (para. 43(b)); section 5 shows the exception."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Foreign-currency cash flows are discounted at a rate for that currency and translated at the spot rate on the test date (para. 54)."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"A pre-tax market rate."},{"type":"text","text":" The discount rate is set before tax and reflects current market assessments of the time value of money and the risks not already in the cash flows (para. 55). It is the return investors would require for cash flows of the same amount, timing and risk, often estimated from the weighted average cost of capital (WACC) of comparable listed entities (para. 56)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), a block's net entitlement production is 6,000 thousand barrels in 2025, declining 10 percent a year, and the contract ends after 2029. Prices follow PHE's 2024 ICP (Indonesian Crude Price) assumption of USD 73.73 to 81.56 per barrel (Note 17, Daftar 5/111, PDF p. 128). Operating and maintenance spending is USD 30 per barrel. The rate is 10.00 percent, PHE's 2024 rate. Cash flow = production × (price − 30)."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Year"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Production (thousand bbl)"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Price (USD/bbl)"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cash flow"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Discount factor at 10%"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Present value"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2025"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"6,000.0"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"73.73"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"262,380.0"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"0.90909"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"238,527.3"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2026"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"5,400.0"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"74.55"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"240,570.0"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"0.82645"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"198,818.2"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2027"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4,860.0"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"76.02"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"223,657.2"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"0.75131"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"168,037.0"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2028"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4,374.0"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"79.07"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"214,632.2"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"0.68301"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"146,596.7"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2029"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3,936.6"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"81.56"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"202,971.1"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"0.62092"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"126,029.1"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"VIU"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"878,008"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"If the block is carried at 900,000:"}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Impairment loss at 10.00% = 900,000 − 878,008 = 21,992"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"At PHE's 2023 rate of 9.45%, VIU = 889,923 and the loss = 10,077"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"At 10.00% with every price USD 5 lower, VIU = 783,005 and the loss = 116,995"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A rise of 0.55 points in the rate costs 11,915 of value; a USD 5 cut in the price path costs 95,003. That is why the standard calls the price path and the rate "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"key assumptions"},{"type":"text","text":", those to which recoverable amount is most sensitive (para. 134(d))."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"5. Cash-generating units"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A well, a pipeline and a platform cannot each be valued on their own, because none of them sells oil alone. When an asset's recoverable amount cannot be estimated individually, it is estimated for its "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"cash-generating unit"},{"type":"text","text":", the smallest identifiable group of assets whose cash inflows are largely independent of those of other assets (paras. 6, 66)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Identifying a CGU is judgement (para. 68), and the standard gives three guides. The entity looks at how management monitors operations and decides what to keep or sell (para. 69). If an active market exists for the output of a group of assets, that group is a CGU even if the output is used internally (para. 70). And CGUs are identified consistently from period to period (para. 72). In the standard's own example, a bus company obliged by contract to run five routes has one CGU for all five, because it cannot close the loss-making route alone (para. 68). In an upstream group the usual unit is the contract area. PHE treats its participating interest in each block as one CGU (Note 17, Daftar 5/110, PDF p. 127)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Carrying amount on the same basis."},{"type":"text","text":" The CGU's carrying amount must be built the same way as its recoverable amount (para. 75). It normally excludes recognised liabilities, but when a buyer would have to take a liability over, the liability is deducted from both sides (para. 78). Upstream, the decommissioning provision is the main case."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), a block is carried at 800,000, which includes capitalised decommissioning cost, and the decommissioning provision is 200,000. A buyer offers 580,000 and would take over the obligation; disposal costs are negligible. VIU before decommissioning outflows is 750,000."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"FVLCD = 580,000 (already net of the obligation)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"VIU = 750,000 − 200,000 = 550,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Carrying amount of the CGU = 800,000 − 200,000 = 600,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Impairment loss = 600,000 − higher of (580,000, 550,000) = 20,000"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Comparing the 580,000 offer with the gross 800,000 would show a loss of 220,000, charging the obligation against the block while the provision stays on the balance sheet."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"6. Recognising and allocating an impairment loss"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For an individual asset at cost, the loss is the shortfall and goes to profit or loss immediately (paras. 59–60). Later depreciation is recomputed on the reduced carrying amount over the remaining life (para. 63), and deferred tax is recomputed against the new carrying amount (para. 64). For a revalued asset the loss is first charged against that asset's revaluation surplus in other comprehensive income (para. 61). A loss of 20 on land with a surplus of 15 is Dr Revaluation surplus (OCI) 15, Dr Impairment loss 5 / Cr Land 20."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The loss may be credited directly to the asset or to an "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"allowance for impairment"},{"type":"text","text":", a contra account. PHE uses the allowance (\"penyisihan penurunan nilai\") inside each asset's movement table (Note 17), so cost stays visible, and names the expense \"provision for impairment of non-financial assets\"; this page calls it "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"impairment loss"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Allocation within a CGU."},{"type":"text","text":" A CGU's loss must be spread over its assets in a fixed order (para. 104). It goes first to any goodwill allocated to the unit, then to the other assets pro rata to their carrying amounts. No asset may go below the highest of its FVLCD, its VIU and zero, and what cannot be absorbed is reallocated to the others (para. 105). PHE's Note 17 block tables carry a goodwill column for this first step, nil for every impaired block."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), a block CGU holds goodwill 20,000, wells 300,000, installations 150,000 and a field office with camp 50,000 whose FVLCD is 48,000. Recoverable amount is 400,000."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Carrying amount = 20,000 + 300,000 + 150,000 + 50,000 = 520,000; loss = 520,000 − 400,000 = 120,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Step 1, goodwill: 20,000; remaining 100,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Step 2, pro rata over 500,000: wells 60,000, installations 30,000, office 10,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Step 3, floor: the office can lose only 50,000 − 48,000 = 2,000; the other 8,000 goes to wells and installations 300 : 150"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wells = 60,000 + 8,000 × 300/450 = 65,333; installations = 30,000 + 8,000 × 150/450 = 32,667"}]}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Debit"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Credit"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Impairment loss 120,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Allowance for impairment, goodwill 20,000"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Allowance for impairment, wells 65,333"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Allowance for impairment, installations 32,667"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Allowance for impairment, field office 2,000"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"7. Goodwill and corporate assets"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Goodwill and head-office assets produce no cash flows of their own, so neither can be tested alone. Both are pushed down into CGUs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Goodwill."},{"type":"text","text":" From the acquisition date goodwill is allocated to the CGUs, or groups of CGUs, expected to benefit from the combination's synergies, at the lowest level at which management monitors it and never above an operating segment (para. 80). Each unit carrying goodwill is tested every year, at the same time each year, and whenever there is an indication (paras. 90, 96), after the assets and smaller units inside it (paras. 97–98). How goodwill arises and is first measured is taught in the Intangible Assets essay."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Corporate assets."},{"type":"text","text":" A headquarters building, a data centre or a research facility contributes to several CGUs. Where a portion can be allocated on a reasonable and consistent basis, each CGU is tested with its share; otherwise the CGU is tested alone and the corporate asset is tested with the smallest group of CGUs it can be allocated to (para. 102)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), a regional office carried at 60,000 serves three blocks carried at 200,000 (A), 300,000 (B) and 500,000 (C), and is allocated by carrying amount. Recoverable amounts are 230,000, 290,000 and 560,000."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Shares of the office: A 12,000, B 18,000, C 30,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A: 212,000 < 230,000, no loss; C: 530,000 < 560,000, no loss"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"B: 318,000 − 290,000 = 28,000 loss; to block B assets 28,000 × 300/318 = 26,415 and to the office 28,000 × 18/318 = 1,585"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Without the office share, block B (300,000 against 290,000) would show a loss of only 10,000."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"8. Reversing an impairment loss"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Impairment losses rest on estimates, so they can come back. At each reporting date the entity asks whether a past loss on any asset other than goodwill may have decreased, using indications that mirror those of section 2: higher prices, lower market rates, favourable changes in how the asset is used (paras. 110–111). A loss is reversed only if the estimates used to measure recoverable amount have changed (para. 114). VIU rises every year because the cash flows come closer, and that unwinding of the discount is not a reason to reverse (para. 116)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The reversal has a ceiling. The new carrying amount may not exceed what the carrying amount would have been, net of depreciation, had no loss been recognised (para. 117). The reversal goes to profit or loss unless the asset is revalued (para. 119), and depreciation is recomputed afterwards (para. 121). For a CGU the reversal is spread pro rata over its assets except goodwill (para. 122). Goodwill impairment is never reversed (para. 124), because a later rise in the unit's value is likely to be internally generated goodwill, which may not be recognised (para. 125). An impairment of goodwill booked at an interim date is not reversed at year end either (ISAK 110, formerly ISAK 17, IFRIC 10)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), take a block with no earlier impairment, carried at 369,670 and written down to 305,466, the 2024 figures for East Kalimantan and Attaka. Suppose it depletes one fifth of its remaining carrying amount in 2025 and, at the end of 2025, a higher price forecast lifts its recoverable amount to 320,000."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Carrying amount after impairment and 2025 depletion = 305,466 × 4/5 = 244,373"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Carrying amount had there been no impairment = 369,670 × 4/5 = 295,736"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reversal = 295,736 − 244,373 = 51,363 (the uncapped 320,000 − 244,373 = 75,627 is not allowed)"}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Allowance for impairment, oil and gas properties 51,363 / Cr Reversal of impairment loss 51,363"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PHE's real block was also impaired in 2023, as the PHKT block (92,607; Daftar 5/112, PDF p. 129), so its ceiling would add that loss back too, net of the depletion it would have borne."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"9. Exploration and evaluation assets"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Exploration assets are tested under a modified regime. PSAK 106 (formerly PSAK 64, IFRS 6) replaces the indications of section 2 with its own list: an expiring exploration right, no further substantive exploration budgeted, no commercially viable discovery, or a development unlikely to recover the E&E cost in full (paras. 18–20). E&E assets may be grouped into CGUs no larger than an operating segment (para. 21), and they are tested before they are reclassified to development (para. 17). Measurement follows PSAK 236; the Oil and Gas Properties essay covers the E&E test in full."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"10. Impairment across industries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Mining."},{"type":"text","text":" A coal or nickel miner tests a mine as a CGU with the same inputs as an oil field (a commodity price path, reserves, cost per tonne and a discount rate) and treats its restoration provision as in section 5."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Plantations."},{"type":"text","text":" Oil palms are "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"bearer plants"},{"type":"text","text":", fixed assets under PSAK 216, and so fall under PSAK 236; the fresh fruit bunches growing on them are biological assets at fair value less costs to sell under PSAK 241 and are outside it. The CGU question turns on para. 70. An estate that sends all its bunches to the group's own mill is still a separate CGU if bunches trade in an active market, and its VIU must use market prices for bunches, not the internal transfer price."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Telecom towers."},{"type":"text","text":" Tenancy contracts often cover many towers at once, so a single tower's inflows are rarely independent and towers are grouped. Falling tenancy per tower is the usual indicator."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Retail stores."},{"type":"text","text":" Each store is often a CGU, since management decides store by store whether to close. Under PSAK 116 the store's right-of-use asset sits inside the CGU, and the lease liability is excluded unless it is deducted on both sides. For example (illustration), a store with leasehold improvements of 2,000 and a right-of-use asset of 6,000 has a VIU, before lease payments, of 7,000. The loss is 8,000 − 7,000 = 1,000. Deducting the lease liability of 6,500 from both sides gives 1,500 − 500 = 1,000 as well, which is the point of paras. 78–79."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Shipping."},{"type":"text","text":" A vessel usually is its own CGU when it trades on the spot market. For example (illustration), a tanker carried at 40,000 has a broker value of 31,000 less 500 of selling costs and a VIU of 34,000. Recoverable amount is 34,000 and the loss 6,000."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11. Presentation and analysis: PHE's Notes 12, 16, 17 and 46"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PHE's 215,666 comes from Notes 17 and 12; Notes 16 and 13 report none, and the segment note confirms the total. PSAK 236 asks for this by class, segment and material CGU (paras. 126, 129–130)."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2024"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Source"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Amount"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Oil and gas properties, new impairment"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 17, Daftar 5/109 (PDF p. 126)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"220,899"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Oil and gas properties, \"deductions\" column, netted in the charge per Note 46"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 17"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(5,350)"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed assets"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 12, Daftar 5/100–5/101 (PDF pp. 117–118)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"117"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Investments in oil and gas blocks (Malaysia, Iraq)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 16, Daftar 5/107 (PDF p. 124)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"nil"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Total = segment note: exploration and production 215,549 + services 117"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 46, Daftar 5/220 (PDF p. 237)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"215,666"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 17 lists the six impaired blocks (Daftar 5/111, PDF p. 128)."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Block (2024)"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Recoverable amount"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Carrying amount"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Loss"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Recoverable / carrying"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Mahakam"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,115,269"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,256,237"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"140,968"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"88.8%"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"East Kalimantan and Attaka"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"305,466"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"369,670"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"64,204"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"82.6%"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Simenggaris"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"–"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"10,815"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"10,815"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"0%"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ogan Komering"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"7,293"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"10,768"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3,475"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"67.7%"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"West Madura Offshore"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"62,167"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"63,201"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,034"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"98.4%"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Raja Tempirai"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"–"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"403"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"403"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"0%"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Total"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"1,490,195"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"1,711,094"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"220,899"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"87.1%"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Mahakam and East Kalimantan and Attaka = (140,968 + 64,204) / 220,899 = 92.9% of the oil and gas charge"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Oil and gas charge, net / opening carrying amount = 215,549 / 16,130,290 = 1.3% (2023: 707,087 / 15,371,796 = 4.6%)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Allowance for impairment / cost of oil and gas properties = 2,242,412 / 41,972,216 = 5.3% (2023: 2,132,390 / 37,777,915 = 5.6%)"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The disclosed key assumptions are the ICP path (USD 73.73 in 2025 rising to 81.56 in 2029, then by USD 0.30–2.99 a year), gas at contract prices, and a discount rate of 10.00 percent against 9.45 percent in 2023 (Note 17, Daftar 5/111, PDF p. 128). The indicators, listed for 2024 and 2023 together, include a lower ICP and higher WACC assumption, natural decline, and large additions at PHM (Mahakam) and PHKT that do not lengthen field life; the NSO reserve downgrade and the Nunukan delay match blocks impaired in 2023 (Daftar 5/110 and 5/112, PDF pp. 127, 129). Mahakam and PHKT were impaired in both years (270,827 and 92,607 in 2023). The note does not say whether recoverable amounts are VIU or FVLCD, and it calls the rate a WACC assumption without saying whether it is pre-tax. Para. 134, with the sensitivity of 134(f), applies to CGUs carrying significant goodwill. PHE's remaining goodwill (ONWJ, Note 13, Daftar 5/104, PDF p. 121) is small against the group, and PHE gives no such disclosure."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"12. Upstream note: what the contract does to the test"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A PSC block has a fixed term, so VIU runs to the earlier of the end of economic production and the end of the contract; an extension enters only if it is supportable, with greater weight on external evidence (para. 33(a)). The cash flows are the contractor's entitlement: cost recovery plus its share of the remaining production, less the crude it must supply to the domestic market at the DMO price (Note 2a(iii)–(v), Daftar 5/10, PDF p. 27). That is why the price path and the cost base enter the test together."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"13. Related lines"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/oil-gas-properties-net","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"oil-gas-properties-net"},{"type":"text","text":": the allowance for impairment of 2,242,412 and the E&E test."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/fixed-assets-net","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"fixed-assets-net"},{"type":"text","text":": the allowance of 5,449 and the reversal mechanics on a single asset."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/intangible-assets-net","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"intangible-assets-net"},{"type":"text","text":": goodwill, its allocation to CGUs and the annual test."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/long-term-investments","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"long-term-investments"},{"type":"text","text":": the Malaysian and Iraqi block investments and associates tested under PSAK 236."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/oil-gas-properties-net","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"depreciation-depletion-amortization"},{"type":"text","text":": the charge that falls after an impairment and rises after a reversal."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/decommissioning-site-restoration-provision","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"decommissioning-site-restoration-provision"},{"type":"text","text":": the liability that must be treated consistently in a CGU test."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/right-of-use-assets-net","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"right-of-use-assets-net"},{"type":"text","text":": leased assets inside a CGU."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Least-confident assertions"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 215,666 reconciles only if the 5,350 in the \"deductions\" column of Note 17's allowance reduces the charge, as the segment note's 215,549 implies. Note 17 does not label it as a reversal, and two features weigh against one. The 5,350 sits in the deductions column with derecognised cost (304,224) and accumulated DD&A (21,382), and the block table's recovery column shows none. If it is allowance released on derecognised assets, netting it in the impairment line understates the charge by 5,350."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 2023 line (707,087) equals Note 17's oil and gas impairment alone. Note 12 reports a 2023 fixed-asset impairment of 319 and Note 16 one of 2,263 on the Malaysian block investment, and neither appears in the 2023 line or in the segment note. The 2,263 probably sits in the 2023 DD&A line, which cites Note 16a and exceeds its identifiable components by 2,267 (the reconciliation in the Oil and Gas Properties essay). No home for the 319 was found."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 17 has internal slips. The English text gives the 2024 loss as US$257,554 against 220,899 in the Indonesian text and the table, both languages say the test was performed \"on 31 December 2023\" in the 2024 note, the 2023 block table totals 707,088 against 707,087, and policy 3m refers to impairment \"Note 2w\" where the policy is 3w. The \"corrections\" column of the allowance (+105,527) is not explained."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"That the 2023 \"PHKT block\" is the 2024 \"East Kalimantan and Attaka\" block is read from Note 1, where PHKT holds the East Kalimantan block; Note 17 uses different names in the two years."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The upstream points in section 12 (contract term as the VIU horizon, entitlement cash flows) are this page's application of paras. 33 and 39 to a PSC. PHE does not describe how its cash flows are built."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The industry practices in section 10 (tower grouping, store-level CGUs, vessel CGUs) are common practice described from knowledge, not from a named company's statements."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"References"}]},{"type":"orderedList","attrs":{"start":1,"type":null},"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PT Pertamina Hulu Energi dan Entitas Anak, consolidated financial statements 31 December 2024 (audited, USD thousand): statement of profit or loss (Daftar 2/1, PDF p. 14); Note 3m (Daftar 5/56–5/57, PDF pp. 73–74); Note 3w (Daftar 5/72–5/73, PDF pp. 89–90); Note 4b(iv) (Daftar 5/82, PDF p. 99); Note 2a(iii)–(v) (Daftar 5/10, PDF p. 27); Note 12 (Daftar 5/100–5/101, PDF pp. 117–118); Note 13 (Daftar 5/104, PDF p. 121); Note 16 (Daftar 5/107, PDF p. 124); Note 17 (Daftar 5/109–5/112, PDF pp. 126–129); Note 46 (Daftar 5/220–5/221, PDF pp. 237–238). VERIFIED (PHE FS 2024, on disk; line totals checked to the PHE FS 2024 data extract)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"No lecture note in this series covers impairment as a chapter. The owner's notes have no Kieso Ch 11 (depreciation, impairment and depletion); Inter 1 Ch 12 touches impairment of intangibles and goodwill only. The CA Review 2021 slides in the same folder (Ersa Tri Wahyuni) cover PSAK 48 with a goodwill-first allocation exercise, not used here as a source of examples. Sections 1–8 follow Kieso's impairment sections and the order of the standard. NOTES — NONE EXISTS."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 236 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Penurunan Nilai Aset"},{"type":"text","text":" (IAS 36 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Impairment of Assets"},{"type":"text","text":"), paras. 1–2, 4, 6, 9–10, 12, 14–15, 17–19, 28, 30, 32–33, 39, 43–44, 49–50, 53A, 54–56, 59–64, 66, 68–70, 72, 75, 78, 80, 90, 96–98, 102, 104–105, 110–111, 114, 116–117, 119, 121–126, 129–130, 134. VERIFIED (web, IFRS Foundation text of IAS 36 as reproduced by ICAB, icab.org.bd, 2017 consolidation; the independent recheck confirmed the same paragraphs against the IFRS Foundation bound text). Scope references in that text predate IFRS 9 and IFRS 17; the PSAK equivalents are named from the current list."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"IAI, \"Perubahan Penomoran PSAK dan ISAK dalam SAK Indonesia\" (effective 1 January 2024): PSAK 236, 106, 105, 113, 116, 202, 216, 241, ISAK 110. VERIFIED (web, iaiglobal.or.id). New numbers follow IAS n → PSAK 200+n, IFRS n → PSAK 100+n, IFRIC n → ISAK 100+n; the old numbers (PSAK 48, 64, 58, 68, 73, 14, 16, 69; ISAK 17) are taken from IAI, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Komparasi Perubahan Penomoran PSAK ISAK SAK Indonesia"},{"type":"text","text":". VERIFIED (web, iaiglobal.or.id)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 106 (IFRS 6), paras. 17–21. VERIFIED (web, search excerpts of the IFRS 6 text; the Oil and Gas Properties essay verified the same paragraphs against a full reproduction)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"US GAAP two-step recoverability test and the bar on reversal for assets held and used (ASC 360): from knowledge, STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"IASB Exposure Draft "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Business Combinations — Disclosures, Goodwill and Impairment"},{"type":"text","text":" (March 2024), proposing to drop the pre-tax requirement for VIU among other changes to IAS 36: not mentioned in the body because it was still under redeliberation in 2025–2026 and is not effective. VERIFIED (web, IASB Updates 2025 and staff papers 2026, via search summary)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Kieso, Weygandt and Warfield, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Intermediate Accounting"},{"type":"text","text":", IFRS edition, chs. 11–12 (impairments). Not on disk; NOT VERIFIED."}]}]}]}]}$j$::jsonb
   where e.id = '024cc475-7902-4b1e-ad3f-97e432c92c43'
     and e.section = 'accounting'
     and e.content_json is null
     and md5(e.content) = 'ea13c0c970d2a454fb5d79422d1e565e'
  returning e.id, e.title, e.snippet, e.status, e.content_json
