-- other-taxes-receivable-current-vat-and-withholding: content_json backfill (the document content was serialised from)
with up as (
  update public.essays e
     set content_json = $j${"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"In brief"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Taxes other than income tax fall outside PSAK 212. For each one, the accounting depends on who bears the tax. Tax the entity collects or withholds for the state is a liability. Tax it pays and can recover is a receivable. Tax it pays and cannot recover is part of the cost of what it bought."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Value added tax (VAT) is collected at every stage of a supply chain, and each business pays the state only output VAT less input VAT. When input exceeds output, the business is owed money. It carries the excess forward or claims a refund, and exporters and suppliers to VAT collectors are owed money most months."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"An upstream oil and gas contractor sells crude and piped gas whose supply is exempt from VAT, so it cannot credit its input VAT. Under its production sharing contract (PSC) the government reimburses that VAT out of the state's share of production. At PHE, reimbursable VAT is 505,861 of the 563,451 other taxes receivable at the end of 2024, 475,338 of it in the subsidiaries that hold the PSCs."}]}]}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PT Pertamina Hulu Energi and subsidiaries (PHE) report other taxes receivable, current portion, of 300,738 at 31 December 2024 against 275,612 a year earlier, and a non-current portion of 262,713 against 213,492, in USD thousand (PHE FS 2024, statement of financial position, Daftar 1/1, PDF p. 11; Note 43a, Daftar 5/151, PDF p. 168; \"Daftar\" is the printed page). The current portion is 0.99 percent of total assets and 3.74 percent of current assets (0.89 and 2.79 percent a year earlier); the two portions together, 563,451, are 1.85 percent of total assets. On the other side PHE owes other taxes of 153,068 against 152,476 (Note 43b, Daftar 5/152, PDF p. 169). This page covers all three lines."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"After reading it a student should be able to say who bears each tax, record VAT and withholding from invoice to settlement, measure a disputed or reimbursable claim, and classify it between current and non-current."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"All amounts are in USD thousand unless stated. Figures from PHE's statements are cited to their note. Every other number is labelled an illustration."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. Which taxes are \"other\" taxes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 212 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Income Taxes"},{"type":"text","text":" (formerly PSAK 46, IAS 12) covers taxes based on taxable profit, including taxes withheld on distributions to the entity (para. 2). Everything else is an \"other\" tax, such as VAT, taxes the entity withholds from other people's income, land and building tax ("},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Pajak Bumi dan Bangunan"},{"type":"text","text":", PBB), import duties and regional taxes. Corporate income tax receivable and payable, current and deferred, belong to the Corporate and Dividend Taxes Receivable and Deferred Tax essays."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"No single standard covers other taxes. The accounting comes from asking who bears the tax, and the answer puts the entity in one of three roles."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Role"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Example"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"What the entity records"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Collector or agent: the tax belongs to someone else"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"VAT on its own sales; income tax withheld from employees and suppliers"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"a liability until it pays the state"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Taxpayer who can recover the tax"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"input VAT creditable against output VAT; VAT reimbursed under a PSC"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"a receivable"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Taxpayer who bears the tax"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"input VAT that cannot be credited; PBB; non-recoverable import duties"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"an expense, or part of an asset's cost"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The third row is already written into the asset standards. Inventory cost includes taxes \"other than those subsequently recoverable\" from the tax authority (PSAK 202.11, formerly PSAK 14, IAS 2), and a fixed asset's cost includes non-refundable purchase taxes (PSAK 216.16(a), formerly PSAK 16, IAS 16)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2. Sales tax and VAT: the collector's liability"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A state that wants to tax consumption cannot collect from millions of consumers, so it makes businesses collect for it. The lecture notes, following Kieso's chapter on current liabilities, distinguish a tax on every sale from a tax on value added only. In its usual form a "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"sales tax"},{"type":"text","text":" is charged once, at the retail sale to the consumer. A "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"value added tax"},{"type":"text","text":" is charged at every sale along the chain, and each business deducts the tax it paid on its purchases, so each pays the state tax only on the value it added."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), at the 2024 Indonesian VAT rate of 11 percent, a chemical maker sells to a distributor for 400, the distributor sells to a retailer for 700, and the retailer sells to a consumer for 1,000."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Maker: output VAT = 400 × 11% = 44; pays 44"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Distributor: output VAT = 700 × 11% = 77; input VAT 44; pays 33"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Retailer: output VAT = 1,000 × 11% = 110; input VAT 77; pays 33"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Total paid = 44 + 33 + 33 = 110 = 1,000 × 11%"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"VAT reaches the retail sales tax's total in three payments of 11 percent of each stage's value added (400, 300 and 300). If the retailer evades, the state has still received 77 of the 110."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The retailer's entries, side by side, in the format of the lecture notes:"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sales tax"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"VAT"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Purchase of 700"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Inventories 700 / Cr Cash 700"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Inventories 700, Dr VAT input 77 / Cr Cash 777"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sale of 1,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Cash 1,110 / Cr Sales revenue 1,000, Cr Sales tax payable 110"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Cash 1,110 / Cr Sales revenue 1,000, Cr VAT output 110"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Month end"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(none)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr VAT output 110 / Cr VAT input 77, Cr VAT payable 33"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Payment to the state"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Sales tax payable 110 / Cr Cash 110"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr VAT payable 33 / Cr Cash 33"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Revenue is 1,000 in both columns, because amounts collected for third parties, such as sales taxes, are not part of the transaction price (PSAK 115.47, formerly PSAK 72, IFRS 15). When a till records only the tax-inclusive total, revenue is backed out of it."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Revenue = 1,110 / 1.11 = 1,000; VAT = 1,110 − 1,000 = 110"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"From 2025 the rate is 12 percent, but on a base of 11/12 of the price for non-luxury goods, so the effective rate stays 11 percent (PMK 131/2024)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3. Input VAT, crediting and overpayment"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A VAT-registered business ("},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Pengusaha Kena Pajak"},{"type":"text","text":", PKP) settles VAT by tax period, which in Indonesia is a month. Within each month it credits input VAT against output VAT (UU PPN art. 9). A positive balance is paid to the state. A negative one is an overpayment, and the general rule carries it forward to the next month as a credit ("},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"kompensasi"},{"type":"text","text":"), and a cash refund ("},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"restitusi"},{"type":"text","text":") can be requested only at the end of the financial year (art. 9(4) and (4a)). Some businesses may request a refund every month (art. 9(4b)), among them exporters and those whose sales go to VAT collectors (section 4)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), a chemicals distributor selling to manufacturers records three months."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"January"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"February"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"March"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Output VAT"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"500"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"300"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"450"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Input VAT"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"380"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"520"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"200"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Net for the month"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"120 payable"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"220 overpaid"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"250 payable"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Credit brought forward"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(220)"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Paid to the state"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"120"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"0"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"30"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"January: Dr VAT output 500 / Cr VAT input 380, Cr VAT payable 120"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"February: Dr VAT output 300, Dr VAT overpaid, carried forward 220 / Cr VAT input 520"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"March: Dr VAT output 450 / Cr VAT input 200, Cr VAT overpaid, carried forward 220, Cr VAT payable 30"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 220 at the end of February is a receivable, recovered by paying 220 less in March. At year end a refund request would start a tax examination (see the Corporate and Dividend Taxes Receivable essay)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4. When input VAT cannot be credited, and VAT collectors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Non-creditable input VAT is cost."},{"type":"text","text":" Crediting needs output VAT to credit against. A business whose own supplies are not subject to VAT has none, so the input VAT it pays is a cost like any other part of the price (section 1, third row). PHE's policy, in its Indonesian text, puts VAT that \"tidak dapat dikreditkan\" (cannot be credited) into the cost of the asset or the expense, and carries the net VAT claimed for refund, or owed, as an asset or liability (Note 3s, Daftar 5/70, PDF p. 87). It does not mention reimbursement (section 10). For example (illustration), a company with only exempt supplies buys casing for 1,000 plus VAT of 110."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Inventories 1,110 / Cr Trade payables 1,110"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"VAT collectors."},{"type":"text","text":" Some buyers are appointed "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"pemungut PPN"},{"type":"text","text":", VAT collectors. The supplier still charges VAT and issues a tax invoice, but the buyer withholds the VAT from its payment and pays it to the state itself. Upstream oil and gas contractors and geothermal contractors are such collectors, for purchases above Rp10 million (full amount) including tax (PMK 81/2024, arts. 298–299)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), a contractor buys 2,000 of well services, VAT 2,000 × 11% = 220. For simplicity the buyer books the collected VAT when the invoice arrives, although it collects it on payment."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Buyer (VAT collector)"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Supplier"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Production expenses 2,000, Dr VAT input 220 / Cr Trade payables 2,000, Cr VAT collected, payable 220"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Trade receivables 2,220 / Cr Revenue 2,000, Cr VAT output 220"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Trade payables 2,000 / Cr Cash 2,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Cash 2,000, Dr VAT output 220 / Cr Trade receivables 2,220"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr VAT collected, payable 220 / Cr Cash 220"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The buyer settles the supplier's output VAT, so the supplier has nothing left to credit its own input VAT against. If it paid 130 of input VAT that month, it is overpaid by 130, and next month again, which is why art. 9(4b) lets it claim every month."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"5. Upstream: VAT reimbursement under a PSC"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"An upstream contractor pays VAT on almost everything it buys and charges VAT on almost nothing it sells. Until March 2022, mining and drilling output taken directly from its source was outside VAT (UU PPN art. 4A(2)(a)). The Job Creation Law took coal out of that exclusion in November 2020, and the Harmonised Tax Law (UU 7/2021) deleted the exclusion altogether. Crude oil, piped natural gas and geothermal steam are now taxable goods whose supply is exempt (PP 49/2022, art. 6(2)). Input VAT on exempt supplies cannot be credited (art. 16B(3)), so under section 4's rule it would be a cost."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The PSC changes that. An operating contractor may claim reimbursement of the VAT it has paid on goods and services for its working area, where its contract provides for it. The rules were PMK 218/PMK.02/2014, replaced in August 2019 by PMK 119/PMK.02/2019, which was in turn replaced on 31 December 2024, PHE's balance-sheet date, by PMK 139/2024. The claim goes to SKK Migas, the upstream regulator, which verifies the tax payments with the Directorate General of Taxes (DJP), and the Ministry of Finance pays it from the oil and gas account at Bank Indonesia. Under the 2014 and 2019 texts, three limits decide how much comes back and when."}]},{"type":"orderedList","attrs":{"start":1,"type":null},"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"VAT that was exempt, VAT on LNG plant operating costs, and VAT on procurement that cannot be charged to operating costs are excluded (2014, art. 3(2))."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reimbursement is paid only after the state's share of production from the working area has been received."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"It cannot exceed the state share received. The 2014 text excluded First Tranche Petroleum (FTP), the slice of production taken before cost recovery; from 2019 FTP counts unless the contract excludes it, and the contract prevails where it differs."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"This page has not read PMK 139/2024, so whether these limits still apply is not confirmed. Reimbursement also depends on production. In exploration there is no state share to pay from, and PMK 122/PMK.03/2019 leaves VAT on petroleum operations uncollected (\"tidak dipungut\"), which keeps exploration VAT out of the receivable. Gross split contracts pay income tax under the income tax law (Note 2b, Daftar 5/17, PDF p. 34), and whether reimbursement applies to them was not verified. PHE's label is \"PPN yang dapat ditagihkan kembali\". Other PSC balances with the government belong to the Due from the Government essay."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), a PHE subsidiary in a cost-recovery PSC buys 2,000 of well services, as in section 4, and 300 of catering for a site office, VAT 33. SKK Migas accepts the first and rejects the second as not chargeable to operating costs."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Purchases (as collector): Dr Production expenses 2,000, Dr General and administrative expenses 300, Dr Reimbursable VAT 253 / Cr Trade payables 2,300, Cr VAT collected, payable 253"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Claim rejected: Dr General and administrative expenses 33 / Cr Reimbursable VAT 33"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reimbursement received: Dr Cash 220 / Cr Reimbursable VAT 220"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The rejected 33 is non-creditable VAT, so it becomes cost. The accepted 220 is a receivable because the PSC and the PMK give the operator a right to cash."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"6. Withholding taxes: the agent's liability"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Kieso's chapter lists "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"payroll deductions"},{"type":"text","text":" among current liabilities. The employer subtracts the employee's income tax and social security contributions from gross pay and holds them until it pays them over. Indonesian law extends the role beyond payroll. A payer withholds income tax (PPh) under article 21 from employees' pay, article 23 from domestic suppliers of services, interest, dividends and royalties, article 26 from non-residents, and article 4(2) as a final tax on items such as land and building rent and construction. Since 2025 the withheld tax is due by the 15th of the following month (PMK 81/2024, art. 94)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Payroll."},{"type":"text","text":" For example (illustration), a subsidiary's monthly payroll is 10,000 gross; it withholds PPh 21 of 1,500 and employees' social security contributions of 300."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Net pay = 10,000 − 1,500 − 300 = 8,200"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Salaries and wages expense 10,000 / Cr PPh 21 payable 1,500, Cr Social security contributions payable 300, Cr Salaries and wages payable 8,200"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The lecture notes' version of this entry debits salaries and wages payable. The debit is the expense, because the whole 10,000 is the cost of the month's work. The employer's own contributions are a further expense and a separate liability, covered in the Employee Benefits essay."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Suppliers."},{"type":"text","text":" For example (illustration), the subsidiary, a VAT collector, pays a consultant 500 for technical services, with PPh 23 at 2 percent and VAT at 11 percent."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PPh 23 = 500 × 2% = 10; VAT = 500 × 11% = 55; cash to the consultant = 500 + 55 − 10 − 55 = 490"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Invoice: Dr Consultancy expense 500, Dr Reimbursable VAT 55 / Cr Trade payables 555"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Payment: Dr Trade payables 555 / Cr PPh 23 payable 10, Cr VAT collected, payable 55, Cr Cash 490"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Who bears it decides the cost."},{"type":"text","text":" A withholding tax is the payee's tax unless the contract shifts it. For example (illustration), a non-resident engineering firm agrees to a fee of 800 \"net of Indonesian tax\", with PPh 26 at 20 percent and no treaty relief. The payer must gross up the fee."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Gross fee = 800 / (1 − 20%) = 1,000; PPh 26 = 1,000 × 20% = 200"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Engineering services expense 1,000 / Cr PPh 26 payable 200, Cr Cash 800"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"VAT self-assessed on the imported service = 1,000 × 11% = 110: Dr Reimbursable VAT 110 / Cr VAT on foreign services payable 110"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 200 is the payer's cost, though legally it remains the payee's tax. The 110 arises because a business that uses services from abroad pays the VAT itself (UU PPN art. 4(1)(e)); for a PSC contractor it becomes reimbursable VAT."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"7. Disputes, collection letters and levies"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The measurement rule for disputed income tax, ISAK 123 (formerly ISAK 34, IFRIC 23), does not reach other taxes, and Kieso's chapter would treat a possible refund as a contingent asset under PSAK 237 (formerly PSAK 57, IAS 37). The IFRS Interpretations Committee closed that route in January 2019. A payment on a disputed tax other than income tax is an asset, because the entity has a right to a refund if it wins or the payment settles the liability if it loses (see the Corporate and Dividend Taxes Receivable essay). PSAK sets no measurement rule for it; PHE carries such claims net of a provision for impairment."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), take a real case as the starting point. PHE's subsidiary PEP received an underpayment assessment (SKPKB) in 2015 for PPh 23 of 2011 of Rp140,606 million, about 9,136, and contested it to the Supreme Court, which rejected its judicial review on 3 December 2024 (Note 52b, Daftar 5/236–5/237, PDF pp. 253–254). PHE does not say whether PEP paid. Suppose it paid before objecting."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2015 payment: Dr Other taxes receivable, tax on assessment 9,136 / Cr Cash 9,136"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Had it won: Dr Cash 9,136 / Cr Other taxes receivable 9,136, plus interest compensation ("},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"imbalan bunga"},{"type":"text","text":") as income once virtually certain"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lost: Dr Withholding tax expense 9,136 / Cr Other taxes receivable 9,136"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Paying first removes the base for the fine on tax still unpaid when an objection or appeal fails, 30 or 60 percent (UU KUP arts. 25(9) and 27(5d), as amended by UU HPP). A company that judges part way through that it will probably lose writes the receivable down to a provision before the decision. A decision given before the reporting date, even if notified after it, confirms a condition at that date and is an adjusting event (PSAK 210, formerly PSAK 8, IAS 10). The loss belongs in 2024."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"tax collection letter"},{"type":"text","text":" (Surat Tagihan Pajak, STP) for interest or penalties is challenged by a request to cancel and then a lawsuit ("},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"gugatan"},{"type":"text","text":"), as PHE ONWJ did for VAT of 2020 and 2022 (Note 43g, Daftar 5/157–5/160, PDF pp. 174–177)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Levies."},{"type":"text","text":" PBB cannot be recovered, so it is a cost, and the question is when the liability arises. ISAK 121 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Levies"},{"type":"text","text":" (formerly ISAK 30, IFRIC 21) answers that it arises at the activity that triggers the levy under the law, all at once if the trigger is a single date and progressively if it runs over time. The PBB law taxes an object according to its state on 1 January (UU 12/1985 art. 8(2)). For example (illustration), with an annual PBB of 1,200, a quarterly report shows the full 1,200 as an expense in the first quarter and none in the next three, not 300 a quarter. PHE ONWJ disputes PBB assessments for 2017–2020, for example Rp134,090 million of tax and penalties, about 8,600, for 2020 (Note 43g, Daftar 5/157, PDF p. 174)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"8. Presentation: current or non-current, gross or net"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Current or non-current."},{"type":"text","text":" An asset is current when the entity expects to realise it within twelve months (PSAK 201.66, formerly PSAK 1, IAS 1). For reimbursable VAT that depends on verification time, contested items and whether the block's state share can pay the claim. For example (illustration), a subsidiary in early production holds verified claims of 120, and its block's state share over 2025 is expected to be 45."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Current = 45; non-current = 120 − 45 = 75"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Reimbursable VAT, non-current 75 / Cr Reimbursable VAT, current 75"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"No standard settles whether the non-current part is discounted, and PHE does not say."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Gross or net."},{"type":"text","text":" PSAK 201 prohibits offsetting assets and liabilities unless a standard requires or permits it (para. 32). The VAT a contractor has collected is owed to DJP, while its reimbursable VAT is claimed through SKK Migas, so the two are shown gross even when they arise from the same purchase (section 5). Two subsidiaries' balances are not offset either, because neither has a right to settle net."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"9. Other taxes across industries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Exporters."},{"type":"text","text":" Exports carry 0 percent VAT, so output VAT is nil and input VAT is overpaid every month. Exporters may claim every month (art. 9(4b)), and low-risk taxpayers can receive a preliminary refund before examination (art. 9(4c); the implementing rule was replaced by PMK 28/2026 in May 2026). VAT receivable is a standing current asset."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Coal after 2020."},{"type":"text","text":" Before the Job Creation Law, coal was outside VAT, so a coal miner was in section 4's position and its input VAT was cost. From 2 November 2020 coal became taxable, and unlike crude oil and piped gas (section 5) its supply was not exempted. For example (illustration), a miner buys 10,000 of mining services, VAT 1,100."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before November 2020: Dr Mining costs 11,100 / Cr Trade payables 11,100"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"After: Dr Mining costs 10,000, Dr VAT input 1,100 / Cr Trade payables 11,100"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The change cut the miner's production cost by 1,100 per 10,000 of purchases, and a coal exporter became a refund claimant."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Banks and insurers."},{"type":"text","text":" Most financial services are not subject to VAT, so a bank's input VAT on rent, IT and consultants is operating expense, and its other-tax balances are mainly final tax withheld on depositors' interest."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"10. Presentation and analysis: PHE's Note 43a and 43b"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 43a gives the composition (Daftar 5/151, PDF p. 168)."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31 Dec 2024"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31 Dec 2023"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Company: reimbursable VAT"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"30,523"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"20,321"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Company: withholding taxes"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"7"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"799"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Subsidiaries: reimbursable VAT"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"475,338"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"443,287"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Subsidiaries: withholding taxes and VAT due to tax assessments"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"20,826"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"18,121"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Subsidiaries: other taxes receivable"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"47,312"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"17,131"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Less provision for impairment of tax receivable"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(10,555)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(10,555)"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Total other taxes receivable"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"563,451"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"489,104"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-current portion"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(262,713)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(213,492)"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Current portion"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"300,738"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"275,612"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reimbursable VAT = 30,523 + 475,338 = 505,861 (2024); 20,321 + 443,287 = 463,608 (2023); growth 42,253, or 9.1%"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reimbursable VAT / total = 505,861 / 563,451 = 89.8% (2024); 463,608 / 489,104 = 94.8% (2023)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-current / total = 262,713 / 563,451 = 46.6% (2024); 213,492 / 489,104 = 43.6% (2023)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Provision / gross = 10,555 / 574,006 = 1.84% (2024)"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Almost the whole line is reimbursable VAT. The subsidiaries' 475,338 is where section 5's mechanism can apply, since they hold and operate the PSCs (Note 1a, Daftar 5/1–5/2, PDF pp. 18–19). The Company's 30,523 sits at holding level, where no PSC is operated, so it may be an ordinary refund claim on its own supplies; PHE does not say. Nearly half the line is non-current, and PHE gives no reason or split by block. Possible causes are verification time at SKK Migas and the Ministry of Finance, contested items, and blocks whose state share is too small to pay their claims. The \"other\" category rose by 30,181 to 47,312 without explanation, and its English label, \"Other prepaid taxes\", says something different from the Indonesian \"Piutang pajak lainnya\"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 43b gives the payable side (Daftar 5/152, PDF p. 169)."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31 Dec 2024"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31 Dec 2023"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"VAT (Company 310, subsidiaries 94,584)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"94,894"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"94,092"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PPh 21 (Company 5,744, subsidiaries 38,748)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"44,492"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"42,393"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PPh 23, 26, 15 (Company) and 23, 15 (subsidiaries)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"9,542"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"12,421"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PPh 4(2) (Company −84, subsidiaries 2,979)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2,895"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2,136"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PPh 26 and 22 (subsidiaries)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,245"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,434"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Total other taxes payable"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"153,068"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"152,476"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PPh 15 is a deemed-profit tax on shipping and air charter income; PPh 22 is collected on imports and certain purchases. The VAT payable is presumably mostly VAT collected from suppliers under section 4 and not yet paid over, shown gross beside the reimbursable VAT (section 8). The Company's negative PPh 4(2) payable, 84 (87 in 2023), is tax paid over in excess of tax withheld, a receivable left inside liabilities The amount is trivial, but the presentation is the kind of offsetting para. 32 prohibits."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three further points do not reconcile."}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The provision is 10,555 in both years, yet Note 38 shows \"Impairment and correction of tax receivables\" as a credit of 30,803 in 2023 and nil in 2024 (Daftar 5/149, PDF p. 166). The 2023 credit either did not pass through this provision or relates to income tax receivables."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 43g lists PEP's PPh 23 for 2011 as awaiting the judicial review decision (Daftar 5/168, PDF p. 185), while Note 52b says the Supreme Court rejected it on 3 December 2024 (section 7). The amounts for PEP's 2019 VAT assessments also differ between the two notes, and the provision did not move."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"In Note 43g, PHE ONWJ is said to have applied on 21 February 2023 to cancel VAT collection letters that it received in November and December 2023 (Daftar 5/160, PDF p. 177)."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11. Related lines"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"code"}],"text":"other-taxes-receivable-non-current"},{"type":"text","text":": the part of the same claims expected after twelve months, covered on this page."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"code"}],"text":"other-taxes-payable"},{"type":"text","text":": VAT collected and taxes withheld, covered on this page."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/corporate-dividend-taxes-receivable-current","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"corporate-dividend-taxes-receivable-current"},{"type":"text","text":": income tax overpayments, under PSAK 212."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/due-from-government","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"due-from-government"},{"type":"text","text":": other PSC balances with the government."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/production-expenses","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"production-expenses"},{"type":"text","text":": where non-creditable or rejected VAT ends up."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/trade-payables","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"trade-payables"},{"type":"text","text":": the purchases that generate input VAT and withholding."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Least-confident assertions"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The reimbursement rule in force at PHE's year end is PMK 139/2024, effective 31 December 2024, which was not read. The limits given are from the 2014 text (read in full) and a news summary of the 2019 text. Whether the right still rests with the operator, and how the cap now treats FTP, is not confirmed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"That PHE's reimbursable VAT arises under these PMKs is inferred from the label. PHE's VAT policy (Note 3s, Indonesian text) expenses VAT that cannot be credited and does not mention reimbursement, so as written it does not explain the 505,861. The Company's 30,523 may be an ordinary refund claim."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Why 46.6 percent of the line is non-current is not disclosed. The causes listed in section 10 are possibilities, not findings."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The exemption of crude oil, piped gas and geothermal steam was read in PP 49/2022 art. 6(2) on an OCR'd copy (pasal.id); the item letters were not checked against the official PDF."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"No standard sets the measurement of a non-income tax receivable. Carrying it at the amount expected to be recovered, with a provision, follows PHE's practice and the 2019 agenda decision by analogy. Whether PEP paid the 2011 PPh 23 assessment, and so whether a receivable of 9,136 existed to write off, is not disclosed."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"References"}]},{"type":"orderedList","attrs":{"start":1,"type":null},"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PT Pertamina Hulu Energi dan Entitas Anak, consolidated financial statements 31 December 2024 (audited, USD thousand): statement of financial position (Daftar 1/1, PDF p. 11); Note 2b (Daftar 5/17, PDF p. 34); Note 3s, VAT policy (Daftar 5/70, PDF p. 87); Note 38 (Daftar 5/149, PDF p. 166); Note 43a–43b (Daftar 5/151–5/152, PDF pp. 168–169); Note 1a (Daftar 5/1–5/2, PDF pp. 18–19); Note 43g, PHE ONWJ (Daftar 5/157–5/160, PDF pp. 174–177) and PEP (Daftar 5/168, PDF p. 185); Note 52b (Daftar 5/236–5/237, PDF pp. 253–254). VERIFIED (PHE FS 2024, on disk; Indonesian and English columns read; line figures checked against the PHE FS 2024 data extract)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lecture notes this series follows, \"Inter 2 – Chapter 13 – Current Liabilities\" (Rumpun Akuntansi Keuangan), item 8 \"Sales and value added taxes payable\" and item 10a \"Payroll deduction\". NOTES. Three corrections: the notes call both VAT outcomes \"kurang bayar\" (output below input is "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"lebih bayar"},{"type":"text","text":"); their payroll entry debits salaries and wages payable instead of the expense; and their description of sales tax as taxing every sale fits a turnover tax, not a retail sales tax. The notes do not cover crediting, collectors, reimbursement, disputes or presentation; sections 3–9 follow the laws and standards below."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Kieso, Weygandt and Warfield, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Intermediate Accounting, IFRS Edition"},{"type":"text","text":" (Wiley), chapter on current liabilities (sales and value-added taxes payable, payroll deductions), the textbook the lecture notes summarise. Not on disk; NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"VAT reimbursement to upstream contractors. PMK 218/PMK.02/2014, arts. 1–3, 7, 9: VERIFIED (web, full text at jdih.kemenkeu.go.id), revoked in 2019. PMK 158/PMK.02/2016 (amendment): existence only, revoked in 2019. PMK 119/PMK.02/2019, in force 16 Aug 2019 to 31 Dec 2024, revoking both: status VERIFIED (web, peraturan.bpk.go.id); cap on the state share including FTP unless the contract excludes it, and the contract prevailing: VERIFIED (web, secondary: DDTCNews). PMK 139/2024, effective 31 Dec 2024, revoking PMK 119/2019: status and abstract VERIFIED (web, peraturan.bpk.go.id); text NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PMK 81/2024: arts. 298–299 (oil, gas and geothermal contractors as VAT collectors; Rp10 million threshold), VERIFIED (web, secondary: Pajakku; DDTCNews); art. 94, payment by the 15th of the following month, VERIFIED (web, secondary: MUC; DDTCNews). PMK 131/2024, 12 percent on a base of 11/12: VERIFIED (web, secondary: pajak.com; Bisnis.com). PMK 122/PMK.03/2019, exploration-stage VAT relief: VERIFIED (web, DJP press release, 30 Aug 2019). PMK 119/2024 on preliminary refunds, revoked by PMK 28/2026 from 1 May 2026: status VERIFIED (web, jdih.kemenkeu.go.id)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"UU PPN (UU 8/1983 as last amended by UU 7/2021 and UU 6/2023), art. 9(4), (4a), (4b): VERIFIED (web, secondary: Ortax; MUC; recheck via pasal.id). Art. 4A(2)(a) and (b) \"dihapus\" by UU 7/2021: VERIFIED (web, pasal.id text of UU 7/2021). Coal taxable from 2 November 2020: VERIFIED (web, secondary: DDTCNews; Kontan). PP 49/2022 art. 6(2) items s–t, exempt supply of crude oil, piped gas, geothermal, LNG and CNG: VERIFIED (web, pasal.id OCR text). Arts. 4(1)(e) and 16B(3): STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED. UU KUP arts. 25(9) and 27(5d), 30 and 60 percent fines after UU HPP: VERIFIED (web, secondary: DDTCNews). UU 12/1985 (PBB) art. 8(2), 1 January: VERIFIED (web, secondary: Wikisource; Ortax). Withholding rates under PPh arts. 23 (2 and 15 percent) and 26 (20 percent): VERIFIED (web, pajak.go.id) for art. 23; art. 26 STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 212 (IAS 12) para. 2; PSAK 202 (IAS 2) para. 11; PSAK 216 (IAS 16) para. 16(a); PSAK 115 (IFRS 15) para. 47; PSAK 201 (IAS 1) paras. 32, 66; PSAK 210 (IAS 10); PSAK 237 (IAS 37); ISAK 123 (IFRIC 23). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED for this page (PSAK 202.11 and 201.66 were verified for the Inventories and Corporate and Dividend Taxes essays). ISAK 121 (IFRIC 21) "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Levies"},{"type":"text","text":", obligating event and point-in-time versus progressive recognition: VERIFIED (web, IAS Plus summary). IFRS Interpretations Committee, \"Deposits relating to taxes other than income tax (IAS 37)\", January 2019: VERIFIED (via the Corporate and Dividend Taxes Receivable essay, ifrs.org)."}]}]}]}]}$j$::jsonb
