-- restricted-cash-access-test-classification-and-funds: content_json backfill (the document content was serialised from)
with up as (
  update public.essays e
     set content_json = $j${"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"In brief"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A bank balance leaves cash and cash equivalents only when the entity cannot withdraw it on demand. A contract that limits what the money may be spent on is not enough; a bank that blocks it, or a third party whose consent each withdrawal needs, is."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Restricted cash is current or non-current according to when the restriction lifts or the money is applied to what it secures. Paying into a restricted account is a cash flow; interest credited inside it, a reclassification, or a payment straight from it to a supplier is not."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A fund set aside for an obligation stays on the asset side, gross of the obligation. No standard lets the two be netted, and in Indonesian upstream contracts the fund sits in a joint account with SKK Migas that the contractor cannot draw alone."}]}]}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PT Pertamina Hulu Energi and subsidiaries (PHE) report restricted cash of 154,217 (current) and 1,890,493 (non-current) at 31 December 2024, against 133,537 and 1,700,675 a year earlier, in USD thousand (PHE FS 2024, statement of financial position, Daftar 1/1, PDF p. 11; \"Daftar\" is the printed page). Together the two lines are 2,044,710, or 6.7 percent of total assets, up from 1,834,212 and 5.9 percent. The non-current line alone is 92.5 percent of the total. This page uses those balances as the starting point for its examples, and it covers both lines."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"After reading it a student should be able to decide whether a balance is restricted, place it on the right side of the twelve-month line, record its movements, and show them correctly in the cash flow statement."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"All amounts are in USD thousand unless stated. Figures from PHE's statements are cited to their note. Every other number is labelled an illustration. The order follows the chapter on cash in Kieso's "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Intermediate Accounting"},{"type":"text","text":" (IFRS edition), on restricted cash and compensating balances, and the structure of PSAK 207 and PSAK 201."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. What makes cash restricted"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"Restricted cash\" is not defined in any standard; it is the label preparers use for balances that fail the definition of cash. PSAK 207 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Statement of Cash Flows"},{"type":"text","text":" (formerly PSAK 2, IAS 7) defines cash as \"cash on hand and demand deposits\" (para. 6), and a demand deposit is one the holder can withdraw at any time. So the question for any balance is whether the entity can get the money out today."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The IFRS Interpretations Committee answered the harder version of that question in April 2022. An entity held a deposit it could withdraw at any time, but had agreed with a third party to keep a set amount in it and use it only for specified purposes. The Committee concluded that such restrictions \"do not result in the deposit no longer being cash, unless those restrictions change the nature of the deposit in a way that it would no longer meet the definition of cash\". Breaking the contract would be a breach, but the bank would still pay. The deposit stays in cash, with disclosure and, if relevant, its own line within cash."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), a PHE subsidiary holds three deposits at 31 December 2024."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Deposit"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Terms"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Can the entity withdraw on demand?"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Line"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(a) 2,000 earmarked for capital spending"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A loan covenant says the money may be used only for a compressor upgrade; the bank pays on any instruction"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cash and cash equivalents, with disclosure"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(b) 4,500 debt service reserve"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"account control agreement"},{"type":"text","text":", among the borrower, the lenders and the account bank, tells the bank to refuse the borrower's withdrawals without lender consent"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Restricted cash"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(c) 11,000 abandonment fund"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A joint account with SKK Migas, the upstream regulator, released only with its approval"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Restricted cash"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cash and cash equivalents include 2,000; restricted cash = 4,500 + 11,000 = 15,500"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The earmark in (a) changes what management may do with the money. It does not change what the bank will do, and only the second matters for the definition."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2. Kinds of restriction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Kieso lists the common reasons cash is set aside, and each fits the access test differently."}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Compensating balances"},{"type":"text","text":": a minimum deposit a lender requires as part of a loan. If the agreement legally blocks it, it is restricted; otherwise it stays in cash and is disclosed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Funds for a specific purpose"},{"type":"text","text":": a plant expansion fund or a bond "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"sinking fund"},{"type":"text","text":", money accumulated to repay a bond. Under Kieso these are investments or other assets, usually non-current."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Collateral"},{"type":"text","text":": cash pledged to a bank as security for a bank guarantee or letter of credit. The bank holds it until the guarantee expires."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Escrow and regulatory funds"},{"type":"text","text":": money held by a third party or in a joint account until a condition is met, such as abandonment funds in upstream oil and gas or reclamation guarantees in mining (section 8)."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A compensating balance also raises the true cost of the loan, because the borrower pays interest on money it cannot use. For example (illustration), a subsidiary borrows 50,000 at 6 percent a year and must keep 5,000 blocked at the lending bank, earning nothing."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Interest paid = 50,000 × 6% = 3,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Money the borrower can use = 50,000 − 5,000 = 45,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Effective cost = 3,000 / 45,000 = 6.67% a year"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 5,000 is shown as restricted cash, and the arrangement is disclosed so a reader can see the 6.67 percent behind the 6 percent."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3. Current or non-current"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Restricted cash is current when, within twelve months of the reporting date, the restriction lifts or the money is applied to the obligation it secures. That follows from PSAK 201 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Presentation of Financial Statements"},{"type":"text","text":" (formerly PSAK 1, IAS 1), which classifies cash as current \"unless the asset is restricted from being exchanged or used to settle a liability for at least twelve months after the reporting period\" (para. 66(d)). Because of the words \"used to settle a liability\", money that will pay an obligation due next year is current even though the entity cannot spend it on anything else."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PHE's policy applies the same idea through the obligation. Restricted cash \"for repayment of currently maturing obligations\" is current, and restricted cash for obligations \"maturing after one year\" is non-current (Note 3f, Daftar 5/38, PDF p. 55)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), an abandonment fund holds 11,000 at 31 December 2024. In November 2024 SKK Migas approved 1,500 of plugging work for 2025, to be paid from the fund. Separately, the debt service reserve of 4,500 from section 1 is released when the loan is repaid on 30 June 2026."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31 Dec 2024"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31 Dec 2025"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Abandonment fund, current (approved for use in the next twelve months)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,500"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Depends on approvals given in 2025"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Abandonment fund, non-current"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11,000 − 1,500 = 9,500"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The remainder"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Debt service reserve"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-current: release is 18 months away"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Current: release is 6 months away"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The debt service reserve crosses the line at 31 December 2025 without any transaction at all. Classification follows the calendar, so a reclassification is never a cash flow."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4. Recording restricted cash"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Restricted cash is measured like any bank balance, at amortised cost, with interest accrued and, for foreign-currency balances, retranslation at the closing rate under PSAK 221 (formerly PSAK 10, IAS 21). The page "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/cash-and-cash-equivalents","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"cash-and-cash-equivalents"},{"type":"text","text":" works both through. What is particular to restricted cash is its life cycle. Money goes in, earns interest inside, and leaves either to settle the obligation or back to the entity."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Take PHE's own deposits as the starting point. The subsidiary PHE OSES paid USD 180,027.96 into its abandonment and site restoration (ASR) fund on 21 May 2024 and USD 172,672.89 on 23 December 2024, each on a letter from SKK Migas setting the semester's placement (Note 45i, Daftar 5/208, PDF p. 225). ASR is the work of plugging wells and removing facilities when a field ends."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Total 2024 placements = 180.0 + 172.7 = 352.7 (USD thousand)"}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"21 May: Dr Restricted cash, non-current (ASR fund) 180.0 / Cr Cash in banks 180.0"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"23 December: Dr Restricted cash, non-current (ASR fund) 172.7 / Cr Cash in banks 172.7"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The rest of the life cycle, for example (illustration), on the fund of section 3. Interest at a constructed 3 percent of the opening balance is credited inside the fund. The approved work programme requires the fund to grow by 1,000 a year from deposits and interest combined, so the deposit is the remainder."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"ASR fund"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2024"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2025"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Opening balance"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"10,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11,000"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Interest at 3% of opening"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"300"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"330"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Deposit from operating account"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,000 − 300 = 700"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,000 − 330 = 670"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Paid to plugging contractor"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"0"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(1,500)"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Closing balance"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"11,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"10,500"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Event, 2025"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Journal"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Interest credited to the fund"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Restricted cash, ASR fund 330 / Cr Finance income 330"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Deposit"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Restricted cash, ASR fund 670 / Cr Cash in banks 670"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fund pays the plugging contractor"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Provision for decommissioning and site restoration 1,500 / Cr Restricted cash, ASR fund 1,500"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The last entry never touches cash in banks. The fund settles the provision directly, which is the reason the money was set aside."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"5. Restricted cash in the cash flow statement"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The cash flow statement explains the change in cash and cash equivalents, so a movement in restricted cash is a cash flow only when it crosses that boundary. Applying this to the fund in section 4:"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Event"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Crosses the cash boundary?"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cash flow statement"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Deposit of 670"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, out of cash in banks"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Outflow, 670"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Interest of 330 credited inside the fund"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"None; deducted as non-cash income in an indirect-method reconciliation"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Payment of 1,500 from the fund to the contractor"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"None; no cash or cash equivalent moves"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reclassification between current and non-current"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Release of a fund back to the operating account"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, into cash in banks"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Inflow"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Which activity the deposit belongs to is a policy choice, applied consistently under PSAK 208 (formerly PSAK 25, IAS 8). Investing is supported because the deposit creates a recognised asset, the condition PSAK 207 sets for investing classification (para. 16). Operating can be argued because the fund pays for a cost of operations, and for a debt service reserve financing can be argued because the account exists only because of the loan. When the fund pays the contractor, no cash or cash equivalent moves, so the payment is not in the statement. PSAK 207 requires investing and financing transactions that do not use cash to be disclosed elsewhere (para. 43); that applies here if the entity classifies decommissioning spending as investing, and disclosure is still useful to the reader if it classifies it as operating."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PHE's direct-method statement has no separate line for placements into or releases from restricted cash (Daftar 4, PDF p. 17), so the 210,498 rise in the two lines in 2024 is not visible on its face."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"6. The fund and the obligation stay gross"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"An ASR fund exists to pay the ASR provision, which invites netting the two. Every route in the standards refuses it."}]},{"type":"orderedList","attrs":{"start":1,"type":null},"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 201 prohibits offsetting assets and liabilities unless a standard requires or permits it (para. 32)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 232 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Financial Instruments: Presentation"},{"type":"text","text":" (formerly PSAK 50, IAS 32) permits offsetting a financial asset and a financial liability only with a legally enforceable right of set-off and an intention to settle net or simultaneously (para. 42). The provision is an obligation to perform work, which falls outside the definition of a financial liability."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 237 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Provisions, Contingent Liabilities and Contingent Assets"},{"type":"text","text":" (formerly PSAK 57, IAS 37) treats a reimbursement from another party as a separate asset, recognised only when virtually certain and capped at the provision (para. 53). A fund built from the entity's own deposits is hard to read as a reimbursement from another party, and even if it were one, it would stay on the asset side."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"IFRIC 5, which deals with interests in decommissioning funds administered separately, has not been adopted in Indonesia. DSAK IAI listed it in June 2022 as not relevant to Indonesian fact patterns."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), the field behind the fund in section 4 carries an ASR provision of 24,000 at the end of 2024 against a fund of 11,000."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Gross presentation: restricted cash 11,000 (assets); provision 24,000 (liabilities)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Netted (not permitted): net liability = 24,000 − 11,000 = 13,000"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Netting would show 13,000 where the field owes 24,000 of work and holds 11,000 of money it cannot spend without SKK Migas approval."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fund's value to a cost recovery contractor also has a ceiling. Under the Indonesian rule in section 10, a surplus left in the fund when a cost recovery contract ends goes to the state, so the contractor benefits from the fund only up to the cost it must incur. The ceiling bites only if the fund, with its interest, ends above the cost actually incurred. Art. 15 first adjusts operating cost for any difference, and Art. 16 deals with what is left at contract end."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"7. Disclosure"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Restricted cash is disclosed because its reader is usually a lender or analyst asking how much cash is free to use. PSAK 207 requires the amount of significant cash balances \"not available for use by the group\", with a commentary by management (para. 48), and the components of cash and cash equivalents with a reconciliation to the balance sheet (para. 45). The 2022 agenda decision adds that an entity should consider liquidity risk disclosures under PSAK 107 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Financial Instruments: Disclosures"},{"type":"text","text":" (formerly PSAK 60, IFRS 7), and further information where these are not enough for users to understand the effect of the restrictions (PSAK 201.31)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A useful note says, for each restricted balance, what it secures, who must consent to its release, when it comes free, and which activity its movements use."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"8. Restricted cash across industries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The access test is the same everywhere. What differs is the obligation behind the money and the forms the regulator allows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Mining."},{"type":"text","text":" Holders of Indonesian mining licences must provide a "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"reclamation guarantee"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"jaminan reklamasi"},{"type":"text","text":") for land disturbed by mining. Under Government Regulation 78 of 2010, the production-stage guarantee could take the form of a joint account or a time deposit at a state bank, a bank guarantee, or an accounting reserve ("},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"cadangan akuntansi"},{"type":"text","text":"), and each form produced a different balance sheet. Since Minister of Energy and Mineral Resources Decision 344/2025 (Kepmen ESDM 344/2025) the form is a time deposit, no longer a bank guarantee (ESDM, as reported in October 2025). For example (illustration), a coal miner's reclamation plan requires a guarantee of 2,000 for the year."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Form under PP 78/2010"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Entry"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Restricted cash"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Joint-account time deposit"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Restricted cash, reclamation guarantee 2,000 / Cr Cash in banks 2,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2,000"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Bank guarantee, with a 20% cash margin required by the bank"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Restricted cash, guarantee margin 400 / Cr Cash in banks 400; the guarantee itself is disclosed"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2,000 × 20% = 400"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Accounting reserve"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"No entry; the company keeps the cash"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"0"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The reclamation provision under PSAK 237 is the same in all three. Only the cash set aside against it differs. Under Kepmen 344/2025 the first row becomes the rule, so the miner shows restricted cash of 2,000 whatever its balance sheet strength."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Project finance."},{"type":"text","text":" Power, toll-road and renewable-energy projects financed on their own cash flows usually keep a "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"debt service reserve account"},{"type":"text","text":" (DSRA) holding several months of loan payments, controlled by the lenders. For example (illustration), a geothermal project pays 24,000 a year in principal and interest, and its loan requires six months in reserve."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"DSRA = 24,000 × 6 / 12 = 12,000"}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"At financial close: Dr Restricted cash, DSRA 12,000 / Cr Cash in banks 12,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Final six months, paid from the DSRA: Dr Bank loans (principal) and Dr Interest payable, together 12,000 / Cr Restricted cash, DSRA 12,000"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The final entry is a financing transaction that uses no cash and cash equivalents, so it is disclosed rather than shown as a flow (para. 43), and the repayment appears as a non-cash change in the reconciliation of liabilities from financing activities (paras. 44A–44E)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Property developers."},{"type":"text","text":" When an Indonesian developer sells a house through a bank mortgage ("},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"kredit pemilikan rumah"},{"type":"text","text":", KPR) before the title certificate or the building is ready, the bank commonly holds back part of the loan until the developer delivers. Where the held amount sits in a blocked account in the developer's name, it is restricted cash, current or non-current according to when delivery is expected. For example (illustration), on a house sold for IDR 1,000 million with a 10 percent holdback, IDR 100 million is restricted until the certificate is handed over."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Groups with subsidiaries under exchange controls."},{"type":"text","text":" Cash that local law keeps inside a country is a contrast case. The subsidiary can withdraw it, so it remains cash; it is the group that cannot use it, and PSAK 207 requires that to be disclosed (para. 48) while the balance stays in cash."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Guarantee collateral in service contracts."},{"type":"text","text":" Cash pledged as collateral for guarantees is the most common restricted balance outside regulated funds. PHE's subsidiaries PDSI and PT Badak NGL hold current restricted cash \"as collateral for bank guarantees in relation to the Group's drilling rig contracts and project with customer\" (Note 7, Daftar 5/95, PDF p. 112)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"9. Presentation and analysis: PHE's Note 7"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PHE gives restricted cash by currency, by bank and by purpose (Note 7, Daftar 5/93–5/95, PDF pp. 110–112)."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31 Dec 2024"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31 Dec 2023"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Current, US dollar"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"144,014"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"128,027"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Current, rupiah"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"10,203"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"5,510"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Restricted cash, current"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"154,217"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"133,537"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-current, US dollar"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,886,032"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,650,050"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-current, rupiah"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4,461"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"50,625"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Restricted cash, non-current"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"1,890,493"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"1,700,675"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Total restricted cash"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"2,044,710"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"1,834,212"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The note names four purposes. Restricted cash is ASR funds at ten subsidiaries, including PHR, PHE ONWJ and PHE OSES; the current portion at PHE WMO is gas revenue not yet distributed to SKK Migas and partners; the current portion at PDSI and PT Badak NGL is guarantee collateral; and the current portion elsewhere is deposits required for work programmes and joint studies. Of the total, 1,917,572 (93.8 percent) is held at government-related banks (Note 44b, Daftar 5/182, PDF p. 199). The rupiah share of the non-current line fell from 50,625 to 4,461, leaving it 99.8 percent in dollars."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The note's wording implies that the non-current line is ASR money, which invites a rough comparison with the ASR provision of 3,826,222 (Note 29, Daftar 5/145, PDF p. 162). PHE also holds 66,719 of \"restricted funds for site restoration in joint operation\" within other non-current assets, cash deposited by operators of blocks in which PHE is a partner (Note 14b, Daftar 5/105, PDF p. 122)."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-current restricted cash / ASR provision = 1,890,493 / 3,826,222 = 49.4% (2024); 1,700,675 / 3,784,917 = 44.9% (2023)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Including joint-operation funds = (1,890,493 + 66,719) / 3,826,222 = 51.2% (2024); (1,700,675 + 296,555) / 3,784,917 = 52.8% (2023)"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"On the restricted cash line alone, coverage rose. Including joint-operation funds, it fell slightly. The two move apart because the joint-operation funds dropped by 229,836 while non-current restricted cash rose by 189,818. PHE explains that site restoration funds not yet transferred were moved by SKK Migas and the former operators into the SKK Migas–PHR joint account (Note 14b, Daftar 5/106, PDF p. 123), which may mean part of the rise came from a transfer between lines; the FS do not quantify it. The ratio is rough in any case, because the provision is a present value and the fund a nominal balance, and both are spread across many contracts."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"10. Upstream note: the Indonesian ASR fund"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PHE describes the mechanism in its policy. The group must place ASR funds in restricted bank accounts, \"maintained in joint bank accounts between SKK Migas and the Group\", usable only for ASR \"with approval from SKK Migas\", or \"transferred to SKK Migas if the activities are not conducted by the Group\" (Note 3o, Daftar 5/61, PDF p. 78). That joint signature is why the fund fails the access test."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Minister of Energy and Mineral Resources Regulation 15 of 2018 on post-operation activities sets the rules behind the policy. Funds are reserved in stages under the approved work programme and budget, from the year production is declared commercial, in a joint account at a state-owned bank (Art. 11(2)–(3)); interest counts toward the amount to be reserved (Art. 11(4)). Under a "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"cost recovery"},{"type":"text","text":" contract, in which the contractor recovers approved costs from production before the rest is split with the state, the reserve is a recoverable operating cost (Art. 12(1)); under a "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"gross split"},{"type":"text","text":" contract, with no cost recovery, it is a cost the contractor bears and deducts for tax (Art. 12(2)). A difference between actual cost and the fund adjusts operating cost (Art. 15), and what remains at the end of a cost recovery contract goes to the state, while under gross split it returns to the contractor (Art. 16)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11. Related lines"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/cash-and-cash-equivalents","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"cash-and-cash-equivalents"},{"type":"text","text":": the line restricted balances are taken out of."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/decommissioning-site-restoration-provision","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"decommissioning-site-restoration-provision"},{"type":"text","text":": the obligation the ASR fund exists to pay, presented gross."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/advances-prepayments-current","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"other-non-current-assets"},{"type":"text","text":": holds PHE's share of joint-operation restoration funds."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/long-term-bank-loans-non-current","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"long-term-bank-loans-non-current"},{"type":"text","text":": the loans that debt service reserves and compensating balances secure."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/finance-cost","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"finance-income"},{"type":"text","text":": interest earned inside the funds."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Least-confident assertions"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The provisions of Regulation 15/2018 were checked against the full JDIH text in October 2026 and not reopened for this version; whether the regulation has since been amended was not confirmed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading the non-current line as wholly ASR money, and the 2024 movement as partly a transfer from other non-current assets, rests on the wording of Notes 7 and 14b. PHE does not give a reconciliation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The reclamation-guarantee forms follow Government Regulation 78 of 2010 as summarised by a BPK paper. The change to time deposits under Kepmen ESDM 344/2025 rests on an ESDM official quoted by Dunia Energi (27 October 2025); the decision itself was not opened, so its transitional rules and any remaining forms are not confirmed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The KPR holdback treatment describes a common arrangement; contracts differ, and some developers present the held amount as a receivable from the bank."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The classification of fund deposits, and of decommissioning spending paid from the fund, as investing, operating or financing is presented as a policy choice, and with it whether para. 43 disclosure applies; no survey of Indonesian practice was made."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"References"}]},{"type":"orderedList","attrs":{"start":1,"type":null},"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PT Pertamina Hulu Energi dan Entitas Anak, consolidated financial statements 31 December 2024 (audited, USD thousand): statement of financial position (Daftar 1/1, PDF p. 11); cash flow statement (Daftar 4, PDF p. 17); Note 3f (Daftar 5/38, PDF p. 55); Note 3o (Daftar 5/61, PDF p. 78); Note 7 (Daftar 5/93–5/95, PDF pp. 110–112); Note 14b (Daftar 5/105–5/106, PDF pp. 122–123); Note 29 (Daftar 5/145, PDF p. 162); Note 44b (Daftar 5/182, PDF p. 199); Note 45i (Daftar 5/208, PDF p. 225). VERIFIED (PHE FS 2024, on disk)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"No lecture note in this series covers cash or restricted cash. The order follows Kieso, Weygandt and Warfield, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Intermediate Accounting, IFRS Edition"},{"type":"text","text":", chapter \"Cash and Receivables\" (restricted cash, compensating balances). STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED (textbook not opened)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 207 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Laporan Arus Kas"},{"type":"text","text":" (IAS 7), paras. 6, 16, 43, 45, 48–49. VERIFIED (web, IAS 7 text as published by the IFRS Foundation, copy at moodle2.units.it, opened and extracted). Paras. 44A–44E (reconciliation of liabilities from financing activities) STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"IFRS Interpretations Committee, agenda decision "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Demand Deposits with Restrictions on Use arising from a Contract with a Third Party (IAS 7)"},{"type":"text","text":", April 2022, including its citation of IAS 1 paras. 31, 54(i), 55 and 66(d) and IFRS 7. VERIFIED (web, ifrs.org PDF, opened and extracted)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Minister of Energy and Mineral Resources Regulation 15 of 2018 (Berita Negara 2018 No. 305), Arts. 11, 12, 15, 16. VERIFIED (web, full text, JDIH ESDM PDF, read by the 2026-10-09 recheck)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"IAI/DSAK, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Materi Presentasi Public Hearing DSAK IAI"},{"type":"text","text":", 21 June 2022: IFRIC 5 not adopted, \"tidak relevan dengan pola fakta di Indonesia\". VERIFIED (web, IAI PDF, per the 2026-10-09 recheck)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Government Regulation 78 of 2010 on reclamation and post-mining, forms of reclamation guarantee, as summarised in BPK Perwakilan Kalimantan Selatan, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Tulisan Hukum: Jaminan Reklamasi Pertambangan"},{"type":"text","text":" (2020). VERIFIED (web, secondary source). Kepmen ESDM 344/2025 (time deposit as the form): Dunia Energi, 27 October 2025, quoting an ESDM official, VERIFIED (web, secondary); decision text NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 201 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Penyajian Laporan Keuangan"},{"type":"text","text":" (IAS 1), paras. 31, 32, 66(d); PSAK 232 (IAS 32), para. 42; PSAK 237 (IAS 37), para. 53; PSAK 208 (IAS 8); PSAK 221 (IAS 21); PSAK 107 (IFRS 7). Numbers and titles VERIFIED (web, IAI, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Perubahan Penomoran PSAK dan ISAK dalam SAK Indonesia"},{"type":"text","text":"); para. 66(d) wording VERIFIED (web, via the 2022 agenda decision); other content STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED."}]}]}]}]}$j$::jsonb
