-- retained-earnings-profit-allocation-and-dividends: content_json backfill (the document content was serialised from)
with up as (
  update public.essays e
     set content_json = $j${"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"In brief"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Retained earnings is the part of equity the entity earned rather than received from its owners: cumulative profit attributable to the owners, less what has been distributed, adjusted for corrections of past errors and changes in accounting policy. It is a claim on net assets and can be far larger than the cash on hand."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"In an Indonesian limited company the shareholders' meeting (RUPS) allocates last year's profit. A statutory reserve must be set aside until it reaches 20 percent of issued and paid-up capital, and dividends may be paid only while retained earnings are positive (UU PT arts. 70–71). A cash dividend becomes a liability when it is declared, not when the year ends."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dividends in kind are measured at the fair value of what is given (ISAK 117), share dividends move amounts within equity without changing the total, and a \"dividend\" that exceeds retained earnings returns capital. Banks and cooperatives add their own rules on what may be distributed, and in sharia banks the profit share of mudharabah fund holders comes off before profit reaches the owners."}]}]}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PT Pertamina Hulu Energi and subsidiaries (PHE) report retained earnings of 4,352,620 at 31 December 2024 against 3,430,896 a year earlier, in USD thousand (PHE FS 2024, statement of financial position, Daftar 1/3, PDF p. 13; \"Daftar\" is the printed page). The line is split into appropriated retained earnings of 1,167,892 and unappropriated retained earnings of 3,184,728. It is 14.3 percent of total assets and 30.2 percent of the equity attributable to owners of the parent (11.1 and 25.3 percent a year earlier)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"After reading this page a student should be able to roll retained earnings forward, record each kind of dividend and its dates, apply the Indonesian rules on reserves and distributions, and correct a prior-period error through opening retained earnings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"All amounts are in USD thousand unless stated. Figures from PHE's statements are cited to their note. Every other number is labelled an illustration. Share capital and additional paid-in capital are taught in the Share capital essay, accumulated OCI in the Other comprehensive income essay, and non-controlling interest in its own essay."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. What retained earnings is"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Equity has two sources. "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Contributed capital"},{"type":"text","text":" (paid-in capital) is what owners put in: share capital and share premium. "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Earned capital"},{"type":"text","text":" is what the business generated and kept. The lecture notes call it \"earning capital\" and identify it with retained earnings. PHE's contributed capital is 13,631,466 of share capital less 3,649,862 of negative additional paid-in capital, or 9,981,604 (Daftar 1/3)."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Closing retained earnings = opening retained earnings + profit attributable to owners of the parent − dividends declared ± corrections of prior-period errors and changes in accounting policy ± transfers from other components of equity"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A negative balance is an "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"accumulated deficit"},{"type":"text","text":" (saldo laba negatif or defisit). Profit or loss attributable to non-controlling interests never enters the parent's retained earnings; it goes to the NCI column."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Retained earnings is not cash."},{"type":"text","text":" Profit is measured on the accrual basis and the cash it brings in is spent on wells, debt service and working capital. For example (illustration), a new PHE subsidiary earns profit of 1,000 in its first year, collects all of it in cash, and spends 900 on drilling."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Retained earnings = 0 + 1,000 = 1,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cash = 0 + 1,000 − 900 = 100"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The balance sheet says the owners have left 1,000 in the business. Only 100 of it can be paid out without borrowing or selling assets. At PHE, retained earnings of 4,352,620 sat beside cash of 2,614,318 at the end of 2024 (Daftar 1/1, PDF p. 11)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Closing the books."},{"type":"text","text":" At year end each legal entity closes revenue and expenses to an income summary and the profit to retained earnings (Dr Income summary / Cr Retained earnings). The consolidated 3,001,475 comes from combining the closed ledgers."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2. Allocating profit: what the law and the shareholders decide"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"An entity rarely pays out all it legally may. The lecture notes give four reasons: agreements with creditors to keep part of earnings as protection, laws that block distribution of earnings equal to the cost of treasury shares (an entity's own shares bought back), the wish to smooth dividends across years, and a buffer against losses or errors in measuring profit. Before declaring, management must also look at cash. The notes put it as a test of financial condition: current liabilities will need cash, so a dividend should be paid only if the present and expected financial position supports it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Indonesian company law, UU No. 40/2007 on Limited Liability Companies (UU PT), sets the order."}]},{"type":"orderedList","attrs":{"start":1,"type":null},"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The company must set aside part of each year's net profit as a reserve, but only while it has positive retained earnings, until the reserve reaches at least 20 percent of issued and paid-up capital (art. 70(1)–(3))."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The RUPS decides how net profit is used, including the amount set aside (art. 71(1))."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Net profit after the reserve is distributed as dividends unless the RUPS decides otherwise (art. 71(2))."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dividends may be paid only if the company has positive retained earnings (art. 71(3))."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"UU PT does not say whether the test uses the company's own or its consolidated figures. Prudence points to the company's own retained earnings, because consolidated retained earnings include subsidiaries' profit that the parent can reach only when the subsidiaries pay it up. In practice Indonesian groups, PHE among them (Note 34), allocate consolidated profit attributable to owners."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, take PHE's 2023 profit attributable to owners of the parent, 2,599,686 (Daftar 2/2, PDF p. 15), as what the RUPS in May 2024 had to allocate. Suppose it sets aside 20 percent and distributes the rest."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reserve = 2,599,686 × 20% = 519,937 (rounded)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dividend = 2,599,686 − 519,937 = 2,079,749"}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Retained earnings, unappropriated 2,599,686 / Cr Retained earnings, appropriated 519,937 / Cr Dividends payable 2,079,749"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"These are PHE's actual 2024 movements, declared by the RUPS recorded in a notarial deed of 31 May 2024 (Note 34, Daftar 5/148, PDF p. 165). The reserve entry moves an amount between two columns of retained earnings; only the dividend leaves equity."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3. Cash dividends and their dates"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A cash dividend has three dates, and only two of them carry an entry."}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Declaration date"},{"type":"text","text":": the competent body approves the dividend. From then on the entity has an obligation it cannot withdraw, so it recognises a liability. In an Indonesian company the body is the RUPS for a final dividend, and the board of directors with the board of commissioners' approval for an interim one (UU PT art. 72)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Date of record"},{"type":"text","text":": the register is closed to decide who receives the dividend. No entry."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Payment date"},{"type":"text","text":": cash goes out and the liability is settled."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, the lecture notes' company declares USD 0.50 a share on 1,800,000 shares on 10 June, with a record date of 24 June and payment on 16 July."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"10 June: Dr Dividend 900,000 / Cr Dividend payable 900,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"24 June: no entry"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"16 July: Dr Dividend payable 900,000 / Cr Cash 900,000"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The notes debit an account called \"Dividend\"; closed to retained earnings at year end, it gives the same result as debiting retained earnings directly. A dividends payable account is a current liability because payment follows within weeks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Dividends declared after the reporting date"},{"type":"text","text":" are not a liability at that date, because no obligation existed then (PSAK 210 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Peristiwa setelah Periode Pelaporan"},{"type":"text","text":", formerly PSAK 8, IAS 10, paras. 12–13). They are disclosed. PHE's statements were authorised on 28 March 2025 (Note 1c, Daftar 5/8, PDF p. 25), and Note 52 reports no dividend declared before that date, so a dividend on 2024 profit belongs to the 2025 statements. PHE's policy says the same thing: dividends are recognised as a liability in the period in which they are declared (Note 3x, Daftar 5/73, PDF p. 90)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Interim dividends."},{"type":"text","text":" UU PT art. 72 allows a dividend before the year ends if the articles of association permit it and the company's net assets do not fall below issued and paid-up capital plus the statutory reserve. If the year then ends in a loss, shareholders must return the interim dividend. For example (illustration), a subsidiary has issued capital of 1,000, a statutory reserve of 120 and net assets of 1,400 in September."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Maximum interim dividend = 1,400 − (1,000 + 120) = 280"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"That is a ceiling. The dividend must also not leave the company unable to pay its creditors or disrupt its business (art. 72(3)), and if shareholders do not return an interim dividend after a loss year, the directors and commissioners are jointly liable (art. 72(6))."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4. Property dividends"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"property dividend"},{"type":"text","text":" (dividend in kind) distributes a non-cash asset such as inventory, land or shares in another company. The question is at what amount the distribution reduces retained earnings, and where the difference between the asset's book value and its worth goes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The lecture notes follow Kieso. At declaration the asset is remeasured to fair value with the gain in profit, then the dividend is recorded at fair value. The notes' example has securities with a book value of 1,250,000 and a fair value of 2,000,000, so a gain of 750,000 at declaration and a dividend of 2,000,000."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK follows ISAK 117 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Distribusi Aset Nonkas kepada Pemilik"},{"type":"text","text":" (formerly ISAK 11, IFRIC 17), which works from the liability side."}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dividends payable is recognised when the dividend is authorised and no longer at the entity's discretion, and is measured at the fair value of the assets to be distributed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"It is remeasured at each reporting date and at settlement, with the changes in equity."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"At settlement, the difference between the carrying amount of the assets and the carrying amount of the liability goes to profit or loss as a separate line."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), a listed company whose shares are widely held declares a dividend of land carried at 800 when its fair value is 1,000. At the year end the fair value is 1,050, and at distribution 1,060."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lecture notes (Kieso)"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"ISAK 117"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Declaration"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Land 200 / Cr Gain 200; Dr Retained earnings 1,000 / Cr Property dividend payable 1,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Retained earnings 1,000 / Cr Dividends payable 1,000"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Year end"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Retained earnings 50 / Cr Dividends payable 50"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Distribution"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Property dividend payable 1,000 / Cr Land 1,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Retained earnings 10 / Cr Dividends payable 10; Dr Dividends payable 1,060 / Cr Land 800 / Cr Gain on distribution 260"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Retained earnings reduced by"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,060"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Gain in profit"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"200 at declaration"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"260 at distribution"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Under ISAK 117 the gain waits until the asset leaves, because the land is still the entity's until then. The interpretation excludes distributions where the same party controls the asset before and after. If PHE handed a subsidiary to Pertamina, Pertamina would control that subsidiary before and after the distribution, so ISAK 117 would not apply, and the same exclusion covers a PHE subsidiary distributing to PHE. Practice then usually uses carrying amounts, the logic of PSAK 338 for common-control transactions (see the Share capital essay)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"5. Liquidating dividends"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"liquidating dividend"},{"type":"text","text":" is a distribution not covered by retained earnings, so in substance it returns the owners' capital. The lecture notes' example is a company that pays a \"dividend\" of 1,200,000 when only 900,000 is covered by retained earnings, and records:"}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Retained earnings 900,000 / Dr Share capital – ordinary 300,000 / Cr Dividends payable 1,200,000"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Kieso debits share premium for the 300,000. Under Indonesian law, article 71(3) allows dividends only out of positive retained earnings, so the excess is not a dividend at all. Returning share capital needs a formal capital reduction approved by the RUPS with notice to creditors (UU PT arts. 44–47). Kieso's debit to share premium has no clean Indonesian counterpart either, because share premium is not retained earnings and cannot be paid out as a dividend under art. 71(3). Single-field and single-mine companies meet this at the end of a project's life. Depletion and decommissioning have consumed the asset, and the cash left over exceeds accumulated profit. The receiving investor treats the excess as a return of its investment (see the Long-term investments essay)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"6. Share dividends and share splits"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"share dividend"},{"type":"text","text":" (stock dividend, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"dividen saham"},{"type":"text","text":") gives existing owners new shares pro rata instead of cash. Nothing leaves the entity, and each owner's percentage is unchanged. Part of retained earnings is "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"capitalised"},{"type":"text","text":", moved into share capital, so that it can no longer be distributed. A "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"share split"},{"type":"text","text":" divides each share into more shares of lower par value and moves nothing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), a subsidiary has 10,000,000 shares of USD 1 par (share capital 10,000) and retained earnings of 6,000. It declares a 10 percent share dividend when the shares are worth USD 3 each, or alternatively splits each share in two."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Share dividend at par"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Share dividend at fair value"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2-for-1 split"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Entry"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Retained earnings 1,000 / Cr Share dividend distributable 1,000; on issue Dr Share dividend distributable 1,000 / Cr Share capital 1,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Retained earnings 3,000 / Cr Share capital 1,000 / Cr Share premium 2,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Memorandum only"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Share capital"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"10,000"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Share premium"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"0"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"0"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Retained earnings"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"5,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"6,000"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Total equity"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"16,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"16,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"16,000"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Shares"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11,000,000 at USD 1"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11,000,000 at USD 1"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"20,000,000 at USD 0.50"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The lecture notes use the par method, as Kieso's IFRS edition does; IFRS has no rule on the amount. US GAAP uses fair value for small share dividends, below about 20–25 percent of shares outstanding, on the view that holders see them as income. A share dividend distributable sits in equity, not liabilities, because it will be settled in shares, not assets. Indonesian "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"saham bonus"},{"type":"text","text":" are a different transaction, capitalising share premium rather than retained earnings (Dr Share premium / Cr Share capital). PHE's 2022 split is covered in the Share capital essay."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"7. Appropriations, the statutory reserve and restrictions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"appropriation"},{"type":"text","text":" earmarks part of retained earnings, in Indonesian "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"saldo laba yang telah ditentukan penggunaannya"},{"type":"text","text":", so that it is not seen as available for dividends. It is a transfer within retained earnings. No cash is set aside, and the total does not change. The lecture notes add that many companies show restrictions by note disclosure instead of a separate account."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"The statutory reserve"},{"type":"text","text":" is the one appropriation the law requires. For example, take PHE's issued and paid-up capital, 13,631,466 in its USD records, and its appropriated balance of 1,167,892 (Note 33, Daftar 5/147, PDF p. 164)."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"20% threshold = 13,631,466 × 20% = 2,726,293"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reached so far = 1,167,892 / 2,726,293 = 42.8%"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Remaining = 2,726,293 − 1,167,892 = 1,558,401, or about 3.0 years at 2024's 519,937"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The law states capital in rupiah. PHE's issued capital is Rp198,112,621,170,000 (Note 32), so the legal threshold is about Rp39.6 trillion, and whether the USD comparison above matches the rupiah test depends on the exchange rates used. Until the reserve reaches 20 percent, it may be used only to cover losses that other reserves cannot cover (art. 70(4)). For example (illustration), a subsidiary has an appropriated reserve of 300 and, after a loss year, unappropriated retained earnings of −500. Its RUPS uses the reserve."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Retained earnings, appropriated 300 / Cr Retained earnings, unappropriated 300"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Remaining deficit = −500 + 300 = −200, so no dividend until later profits clear it"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Contractual restrictions."},{"type":"text","text":" Loan agreements often limit distributions directly (a cap on dividends as a share of profit) or indirectly (a minimum net worth or a maximum leverage ratio). For example (illustration), a covenant capping dividends at 50 percent of prior-year profit of 2,000 allows 1,000, although the law would allow 1,600 after a 20 percent reserve. The restriction is disclosed. PHE states that some of its debt instruments impose maximum leverage ratios and that it complied with all externally imposed capital requirements (Note 49f, Daftar 5/235, PDF p. 252)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"8. Corrections of errors and changes in accounting policy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Retained earnings is where past mistakes are fixed. PSAK 208 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Kebijakan Akuntansi, Perubahan Estimasi Akuntansi, dan Kesalahan"},{"type":"text","text":" (formerly PSAK 25, IAS 8) sorts accounting changes into three kinds and treats each differently (the lecture notes for Inter 2 Chapter 22 give the same three)."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Change in accounting policy"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Change in accounting estimate"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Correction of a prior-period error"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Example"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Average cost to FIFO"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Useful life 20 to 25 years"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Depreciation omitted in a prior year"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Method"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Retrospective, unless a new standard's transition rules say otherwise"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Prospective"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Retrospective restatement"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Comparatives restated"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Opening retained earnings of the earliest period shown"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Adjusted for the cumulative effect"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not adjusted"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Adjusted"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"If retrospective application is impracticable, the entity applies the change from the earliest date it can. When a policy change or restatement has a material effect on the opening statement of financial position, a third balance sheet at the start of the comparative period is required (PSAK 201, formerly PSAK 1, IAS 1, para. 40A)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), in 2025 a non-PSC PHE subsidiary taxed at 22 percent finds that it omitted 5,000 of depreciation from its 2023 accounts, although its tax return deducted it, so only deferred tax was misstated. Its 2025 statements show 2024 as the comparative."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Effect on retained earnings = 5,000 × (1 − 22%) = 3,900"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tax effect = 5,000 × 22% = 1,100, a lower deferred tax liability"}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Retained earnings, opening 3,900, Dr Deferred tax liability 1,100 / Cr Accumulated depreciation 5,000"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 2024 column is restated, and the statement of changes in equity shows opening retained earnings at 1 January 2024 as previously reported, the 3,900 correction, and the restated balance. The error belongs to 2023, so 2025 profit is untouched."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The lecture notes' version of this case is a Pertamina refinery whose 2019 depreciation of 250,000 was left out, with tax at 40 percent. They list \"Accumulated depreciation $250.000 decrease\", \"Deffered tax liability $100.000 Increase\" and \"Retained Earnings $150.000 Increase\" under the statement of financial position, and tax expense and net income as \"Increase\" under the income statement. Restating for the omitted depreciation does the opposite. Accumulated depreciation rises by 250,000, the deferred tax liability and tax expense fall by 100,000, and net income and retained earnings fall by 150,000. Only \"Retained earnings ending balance $150.000 Decrease\" has the right sign."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Policy changes work the same way. In the notes' long-term contract example, moving from cost recovery to percentage of completion at the start of 2019 adds 500,000 of pre-tax profit for earlier years, booked as Dr Construction in process 500,000 / Cr Deferred tax liability 200,000 / Cr Retained earnings 300,000. Under PSAK 115 progress measurement follows the contract facts, so this would now be a change in estimate or a correction rather than a free policy choice; the example teaches the mechanics of the cumulative adjustment."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Transfers from OCI."},{"type":"text","text":" Non-recycled OCI items, such as a revaluation surplus, may be transferred directly to retained earnings when the asset is sold or used up (see the Other comprehensive income essay)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"9. Retained earnings across industries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Banks."},{"type":"text","text":" Prudential regulation limits what a bank may distribute. Under POJK No. 17/2023 on bank governance, a bank must have a dividend policy (art. 108), and OJK may order a bank to postpone, limit or prohibit dividends, or to hold a RUPS to cancel one, when the bank needs to strengthen its capital or resolve problems. Retained earnings is the core of a bank's common equity tier 1 capital, so every rupiah paid out lowers its capital ratio."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Insurers."},{"type":"text","text":" Distributions are constrained by OJK's solvency (risk-based capital) requirements, because an insurer's retained earnings back its obligations to policyholders."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Cooperatives."},{"type":"text","text":" A cooperative's profit is "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"sisa hasil usaha"},{"type":"text","text":" (SHU): revenue for the year less costs, depreciation and other obligations including tax. After the reserve, SHU is distributed to members in proportion to the business each did with the cooperative, and part may fund cooperative education and other purposes; the size of the reserve is set by the members' meeting (UU No. 25/1992, art. 45). For example (illustration), SHU of 1,000, a reserve of 25 percent set by the members' meeting, and 40 percent of SHU shared by member transactions."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reserve = 1,000 × 25% = 250"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Member share pool = 1,000 × 40% = 400; a member with 2% of transactions receives 400 × 2% = 8"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The law ties the member's share to use rather than to capital, which is the difference from a company; in practice the articles often also reward members' savings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Sharia entities."},{"type":"text","text":" In a sharia bank, funds placed under a "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"mudharabah"},{"type":"text","text":" (profit-sharing) contract are temporary syirkah funds, presented between liabilities and equity (PSAK 401, formerly PSAK 101). The share of profit paid to those fund holders comes off before profit for the owners, so it never passes through retained earnings, while dividends to shareholders follow UU PT as for any company."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"State-owned groups."},{"type":"text","text":" PHE's dividends go to Pertamina (Persero), its shareholder, and the 2025 reform does not change that step. It changes the level above. In 2024 Pertamina's RUPS decided what Pertamina paid to the state as non-tax state revenue (PNBP). UU No. 1/2025, the third amendment to the SOE Law, gives the new investment agency BPI Danantara the authority to manage the dividends of SOEs and of its investment and operational holdings (art. 3F(2)(a)), so from 2025 SOE dividends flow to Danantara rather than to the state budget."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"10. Presentation and analysis: PHE's statement of changes in equity and Notes 33–34"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The statement of changes in equity reconciles each component of equity, including retrospective adjustments and dividends (PSAK 201, para. 106). PHE's retained earnings columns (Daftar 3, PDF p. 16):"}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Appropriated"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Unappropriated"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Total"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31 December 2022"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"320,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4,175,513"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4,495,513"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dividend declared (Note 34)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(3,664,303)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(3,664,303)"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Statutory reserve and general and investment reserve (Note 33)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"327,955"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(327,955)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Profit attributable to owners"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2,599,686"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2,599,686"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"31 December 2023"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"647,955"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2,782,941"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3,430,896"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dividend declared (Note 34)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(2,079,749)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(2,079,749)"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Statutory reserve and general and investment reserve (Note 33)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"519,937"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(519,937)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Equity adjustment in subsidiaries"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(2)"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"(2)"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Profit attributable to owners"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3,001,475"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3,001,475"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"31 December 2024"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"1,167,892"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"3,184,728"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"4,352,620"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Increase in 2024 = 3,001,475 − 2,079,749 − 2 = 921,724; 3,430,896 + 921,724 = 4,352,620"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 34 dates the dividends by notarial deed, 3,664,303 on 15 May 2023 from 2022 profit and 2,079,749 on 31 May 2024 from 2023 profit. PHE shows no separate dividend payable on either balance sheet."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Payout ratio = dividends / profit attributable to owners of the year allocated = 2,079,749 / 2,599,686 = 80.0%"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reserve ratio = 519,937 / 2,599,686 = 20.0%"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Return on equity (ROE) = 3,001,475 / ((14,433,117 + 13,534,126) / 2) = 3,001,475 / 13,983,621.5 = 21.5%"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 2024 allocations add up to 2023's profit attributable to owners, 20 percent to reserves and 80 percent to the shareholders, Pertamina and Pertamina Pedeve (Note 32). Measured against 2024's own profit the same dividend is 69.3 percent, a figure that mixes two years. Dividends paid in the cash flow statement (2,117,827 and 3,646,979, Daftar 4, PDF p. 17) differ from dividends declared to owners and NCI (2,107,546 and 3,683,184); see Least-confident. Dividends paid of 2,117,827 went out in a year when cash fell by 2,384,682 before exchange effects, the section 1 point at group scale."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11. Upstream note: the \"dividend tax\" in a PSC"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSC contractors are taxed on their taxable income from PSC operations \"at a combined rate comprising corporate income tax and dividend tax\" (Note 2, Daftar 5/9, PDF p. 26). The dividend part, which for a foreign contractor's Indonesian branch is branch profit tax, is charged on after-tax profit whether or not any dividend is declared, so it sits in income tax expense and reduces profit before it reaches retained earnings. A dividend PHE declares to Pertamina is a separate event (see the Corporate and dividend taxes essay)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"12. Related lines"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/share-capital","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"share-capital"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/share-capital","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"additional-paid-in-capital"},{"type":"text","text":": contributed capital, the 20 percent reserve base, and common-control differences."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/other-comprehensive-income","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"other-comprehensive-income"},{"type":"text","text":": accumulated OCI and non-recycled items transferred to retained earnings."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/non-controlling-interest","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"non-controlling-interest"},{"type":"text","text":": the NCI share of profit and the dividends declared to NCI."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/cash-and-cash-equivalents","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"cash-and-cash-equivalents"},{"type":"text","text":": the resource dividends are paid from."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/long-term-bank-loans-non-current","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"long-term-bank-loans-non-current"},{"type":"text","text":": the covenants that restrict distributions."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/corporate-dividend-taxes-receivable-current","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"corporate-dividend-taxes-payable-current"},{"type":"text","text":": the PSC dividend (branch profit) tax."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Least-confident assertions"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 2024 appropriation equals exactly 20 percent of 2023 profit attributable to owners, and the dividend the other 80 percent, which suggests the RUPS allocated the whole of 2023's profit. The 2023 allocation (3,664,303 + 327,955 = 3,992,258) cannot be checked because 2022 is not in these statements, and press reports put PHE's 2022 net profit at about USD 4.6–4.67 billion on an unstated basis. The 183,255 left after each allocation in both years follows arithmetically from the 2024 allocation equalling 2023 profit. If the 2023 allocation was likewise the whole of 2022 profit, that profit was 3,992,258, with 8.2 percent reserved and 91.8 percent paid out."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The appropriated balance of 1,167,892 is labelled \"Statutory reserve and general and investment reserve\" in the statement of changes in equity, while Note 33's Indonesian title is the statutory reserve balance. How much of it is statutory and how much general or investment reserve is not disclosed, so the 42.8 percent progress toward the 20 percent threshold is an upper bound for the statutory part, and it is computed in USD while the law's capital is in rupiah."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 33 gives the 2023 transfer as USD 327,995, but the statement of changes in equity shows 327,955, and 320,000 + 327,955 = 647,955 agrees with the balance sheet. Note 33 is read as a typing slip."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Over 2023–2024 dividends declared to owners and NCI exceed dividends paid by 25,924 (paid exceeded declared by 10,281 in 2024 and fell short by 36,205 in 2023). The 2023 shortfall exceeds that year's NCI declaration of 18,881, so part relates to owners or to a payable brought forward from 2022. No dividend payable appears in Notes 21, 44f or 51, and withholding tax cannot explain the owners' part, because dividends between Indonesian companies are exempt."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"UU PT arts. 70–72 were checked only through secondary sources, and art. 70(4) and arts. 44–47 are from knowledge. UU PT does not say whether arts. 70–71 use separate or consolidated figures; the prudence argument in section 2 is this page's. Who holds Pertamina's shares after UU No. 1/2025 and UU No. 16/2025 (the fourth amendment) was not checked. That a common-control distribution is usually made at carrying amount is practice, not a stated PSAK rule."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"References"}]},{"type":"orderedList","attrs":{"start":1,"type":null},"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PT Pertamina Hulu Energi dan Entitas Anak, consolidated financial statements 31 December 2024 (audited, USD thousand): statement of financial position (Daftar 1/3, PDF p. 13); statement of profit or loss and OCI (Daftar 2/2, PDF p. 15); statement of changes in equity (Daftar 3, PDF p. 16); cash flow statement (Daftar 4, PDF p. 17); Note 1c (Daftar 5/8, PDF p. 25); Note 2 PSC taxation (Daftar 5/9, PDF p. 26); Note 3x (Daftar 5/73, PDF p. 90); cash (Daftar 1/1, PDF p. 11); Notes 32 and 33 (Daftar 5/147, PDF p. 164); Note 34 (Daftar 5/148, PDF p. 165); Note 49f (Daftar 5/235, PDF p. 252); Note 52 (Daftar 5/236–5/238, PDF pp. 253–255, no dividend after the reporting date). VERIFIED (PHE FS 2024, on disk)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lecture notes this series follows, \"Inter 2 – Chapter 15 – Equity\" (Rumpun Akuntansi Keuangan), section C (dividend policy: reasons for retaining, financial condition, cash, property and liquidating dividends, share dividends and splits) and section D (presentation, restrictions, statement of changes in equity, ROE and payout ratio). NOTES. Corrections made here: the property dividend follows ISAK 117 rather than remeasurement at declaration; the liquidating dividend's debit to share capital is set against Kieso's share premium and Indonesian law; closing the notes' \"Dividend\" account to retained earnings is this page's addition. Statutory reserves, interim dividends, ISAK 117 and the industry section have no note."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lecture notes, \"Inter 2 – Chapter 22 – Accounting Changes and Error Analysis\" (Rumpun Akuntansi Keuangan): three approaches, retrospective adjustment of opening retained earnings, the Waskita contract and Pertamina depreciation examples. NOTES. Five of the eight signs in the depreciation example (accumulated depreciation, deferred tax liability, retained earnings on the balance sheet, tax expense, net income) are corrected in section 8; the Waskita case is flagged as no longer a free policy choice under PSAK 115."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK numbers (PSAK 201, 208, 210, 338, 401; ISAK 117 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Distribusi Aset Nonkas kepada Pemilik"},{"type":"text","text":", formerly ISAK 11): VERIFIED (web, IAI, \"Komparasi Perubahan Penomoran PSAK ISAK SAK Indonesia\", May 2024)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"ISAK 117 (IFRIC 17): measurement at fair value, remeasurement through equity, settlement difference in profit or loss as a separate line, common-control scope exclusion. VERIFIED (web, IAS Plus and IFRS Foundation summaries; the scope paragraph's text not seen). PSAK 210 (IAS 10) paras. 12–13, PSAK 201 (IAS 1) paras. 40A and 106, PSAK 208 (IAS 8) retrospective rules: STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"UU No. 40/2007 on Limited Liability Companies, arts. 70(1)–(3), 71(1)–(3), 72 including 72(3) and 72(6): VERIFIED (web, secondary: Hukumonline Klinik, 13 Nov 2020; BP Lawyers; Binus Business Law, 2016). UU No. 6/2023 amended UU PT arts. 1, 7, 32, 109 and added 153A–J, not arts. 44–47 or 70–72: VERIFIED (web, secondary; official annex not opened). Art. 70(4), arts. 44–47, separate versus consolidated basis: NOT VERIFIED. UU No. 1/2025 (third amendment to UU No. 19/2003 on SOEs), arts. 3F(2)(a) and 3AC: VERIFIED (BPK JDIH, peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/314622, official PDF opened; JDIH lists UU No. 16/2025 as a later amendment, not read). The shift of SOE dividends from PNBP to Danantara: VERIFIED (web, secondary: DDTC News; Bisnis.com, 14 Aug 2025). Pertamina's 2024 dividend to the state as PNBP, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"saham bonus"},{"type":"text","text":" from share premium and the US GAAP 20–25 percent share dividend threshold are from knowledge: NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"POJK No. 17/2023 on bank governance, dividend policy (art. 108) and OJK's power to postpone, limit or prohibit dividends: VERIFIED (web, secondary: Kontan, 19 Sep 2023; Bisnis.com, 20–21 Sep 2023); the article for OJK's power not seen. Insurers' risk-based capital rule and banks' regulatory reserves: NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"UU No. 25/1992 on Cooperatives, art. 45 (SHU, reserve set by the members' meeting): VERIFIED (web, secondary: academic articles quoting the text). Current amendment status NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Press reports of PHE's 2022 net profit (Kontan and Beritajatim, Sep 2023; Kabar Bursa, Jan 2024): used only in Least-confident. Unaudited basis."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Kieso, Weygandt and Warfield, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Intermediate Accounting"},{"type":"text","text":", IFRS edition, chs. 15 and 22, the textbook the lecture notes summarise. Not on disk; NOT VERIFIED."}]}]}]}]}$j$::jsonb
