-- revenues-five-steps-psc-entitlement: content_json backfill (the document content was serialised from)
with up as (
  update public.essays e
     set content_json = $j${"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"In brief"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Revenue is income from an entity's ordinary activities. PSAK 115 measures revenue from contracts with customers through five steps: identify the contract, identify the performance obligations, determine the transaction price, allocate it, and recognise revenue when or as control of each promised good or service passes to the customer."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Most of the judgment sits in steps 3 and 5. Variable consideration enters the price only to the extent a significant reversal is highly probable not to occur, and an obligation is satisfied over time only if one of three tests is met; otherwise revenue waits for a point in time."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"An upstream contractor's revenue is the oil and gas it lifts and sells to its customers. When lifting differs from entitlement the gap is settled with the state outside revenue, and barrels sold only on the state's behalf are not revenue at all. Under a cost recovery contract the entitlement itself rises with recoverable cost."}]}]}]},{"type":"horizontalRule"},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PT Pertamina Hulu Energi and subsidiaries (PHE) report revenues of 14,330,340 for 2024 against 14,568,384 for 2023, in USD thousand (PHE FS 2024, statement of profit or loss, Daftar 2/1, PDF p. 14; \"Daftar\" is the printed page). Revenue fell 1.6 percent. It is 0.47 times average total assets of 30,661,936."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"After reading, a student should be able to run a contract through the five steps with journals, separate revenue from gains and from amounts collected for others, and explain what an upstream contractor's revenue measures."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"All amounts are in USD thousand unless stated. Figures from PHE's statements are cited to their note. Every other number is labelled an illustration. Examples taken from the lecture notes keep the notes' figures in full dollars, and the industry illustrations in section 9 are in plain currency units. The standard is PSAK 115 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Pendapatan dari Kontrak dengan Pelanggan"},{"type":"text","text":" (formerly PSAK 72, IFRS 15), effective in Indonesia since 1 January 2020, when it replaced PSAK 23 (revenue), PSAK 34 (construction contracts), PSAK 44 (real estate) and ISAK 10, 21 and 27."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. What revenue is"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 115 defines revenue as income arising in the course of an entity's ordinary activities (Appendix A). The older PSAK 23 definition in the lecture notes for Teori Akuntansi Ch 9, a gross inflow of economic benefits that increases equity other than from owners, gives the two characteristics that matter: an inflow or increase of assets (or a settlement of liabilities), and an origin in the entity's central, continuing operations. The IASB, unlike the FASB, puts revenue and gains under one element, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"income"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The separation still changes the numbers. For example (illustration), a PHE drilling subsidiary sells a used rig carried at 800 for 1,000."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Revenue view (wrong): revenue 1,000, cost 800"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Gain view: Dr Cash 1,000 / Cr Fixed assets 800 / Cr Gain on disposal 200"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Selling rigs is not the subsidiary's business, so 200 appears as a net gain outside revenue."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 115 adds a second filter. It covers only contracts with a "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"customer"},{"type":"text","text":", a party that has contracted to obtain goods or services that are an output of the entity's ordinary activities in exchange for consideration (Appendix A). The TA Ch 9 notes set out the older test, that revenue be realised or realisable and earned. The Inter 2 Ch 18 notes describe the "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"asset-liability approach"},{"type":"text","text":" that replaced it, recognising revenue as contract rights and obligations change. The Deferred revenue essay covers the resulting balances."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2. Step 1: identify the contract"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A contract is an agreement that creates enforceable rights and obligations, in writing, orally or by customary practice. PSAK 115 accounts for it only when all five criteria hold (para. 9): the parties have approved it and are committed; each party's rights can be identified; the payment terms can be identified; it has commercial substance; and collection of the consideration is probable, judged on the customer's ability and intention to pay."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The collectability test stops revenue that will never turn into cash. For example (illustration), if a PHE subsidiary agrees to deliver 1,000 of gas to a buyer already in arrears with no financing, the contract does not yet exist for PSAK 115. Cash received is held as a liability until collection becomes probable, or until the contract ends and the cash is non-refundable."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3. Step 2: identify the performance obligations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"performance obligation"},{"type":"text","text":" is a promise to transfer a distinct good or service, or a series of distinct goods or services that are substantially the same and transfer with the same pattern (para. 22). A good or service is "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"distinct"},{"type":"text","text":" if the customer can benefit from it on its own or with readily available resources, and if the promise is separately identifiable from the other promises in the contract (para. 27). The lecture notes use Airbus selling an aircraft to Garuda for USD 100 million: one obligation, unless the contract adds maintenance, which must then be separated. Their second case, a turbine sold \"ready to use\", has two, the turbine and its installation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Activities the entity must perform to set up a contract are not obligations unless they transfer something to the customer (para. 25). For example (illustration), a PHE drilling subsidiary signs a 90-day drilling contract at a day rate of 30, with a mobilisation fee of 450 paid on signing to bring the rig to site."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Transaction price = 90 × 30 + 450 = 3,150"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Revenue per drilling day = 3,150 / 90 = 35"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"At 31 December, after 40 days: revenue = 40 × 35 = 1,400"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cash and billings = 450 + 40 × 30 = 1,650; contract liability = 1,650 − 1,400 = 250"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Moving the rig gives the customer nothing it can use on its own, so the 450 is not revenue on arrival at site. It is spread over the drilling days, and the 250 still unearned is 450 × 50/90."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"On signing: Dr Cash 450 / Cr Contract liability 450"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Each drilling day: Dr Trade receivables 30, Dr Contract liability 5 / Cr Revenue, drilling services 35"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Daily gas deliveries under a long-term sale, each distinct but identical, form one series obligation."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4. Step 3: determine the transaction price"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"transaction price"},{"type":"text","text":" is the consideration the entity expects to be entitled to for the promised goods or services, excluding amounts collected for third parties such as sales taxes. The lecture notes list four complications, and PSAK 115 adds a constraint to the first."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Variable consideration."},{"type":"text","text":" Discounts, rebates, bonuses, penalties and price concessions make the price depend on future events. The entity estimates it by the "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"expected value"},{"type":"text","text":", the probability-weighted sum, which suits many similar contracts, or the "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"most likely amount"},{"type":"text","text":", which suits a contract with two outcomes (para. 53). The notes' example, a builder with a contract of 100,000 and a completion bonus of 50,000 that falls 10 percent for each week of delay, uses the expected value:"}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"On time: 60% × 150,000 = 90,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"One week late: 30% × 145,000 = 43,500"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two weeks late: 10% × 140,000 = 14,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Transaction price = 147,500"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"The constraint."},{"type":"text","text":" An estimate enters the price only to the extent that it is highly probable a significant reversal of cumulative revenue will not occur once the uncertainty is resolved (para. 56). For example (illustration), the drilling contract in section 3 pays a bonus of 300 if the well is finished within 80 days, and the subsidiary puts the probability at 70 percent."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Expected value"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Most likely amount"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"After the constraint"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Price"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3,150 + 70% × 300 = 3,360"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3,150 + 300 = 3,450"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3,150"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"With two outcomes the most likely amount fits, but a 70 percent chance in untested ground may not be \"highly probable\", so the bonus waits. PHE's policy measures variable consideration at the amount it expects to be entitled to \"less the estimated amount of service performance guarantees to be paid during the contract period\" (Note 3p, Daftar 5/61, PDF p. 78), which treats expected penalties as a reduction of price."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Significant financing component."},{"type":"text","text":" When payment and transfer are far apart, part of the price is interest (paras. 60–65). The notes' example has Pertamina selling a tanker of crude to Shell for a four-year zero-interest note when the market rate is 12 percent:"}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Face value of the note = 1,000,000 × 1.12⁴ = 1,573,519, which the notes round to 1,573,520"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sale: Dr Notes receivable 1,000,000 / Cr Sales revenue 1,000,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Interest to 31 December 2019: 1,000,000 × 12% × 6/12 = 60,000; 2020: 1,060,000 × 12% = 127,200"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Revenue is the cash-equivalent price, and the rest is interest income, presented apart from revenue (para. 65). The prepayment case is in the Deferred revenue essay."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Non-cash consideration"},{"type":"text","text":", such as the notes' shares received for consulting, is measured at fair value (para. 66)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Consideration payable to a customer"},{"type":"text","text":", such as a rebate, coupon or a payment the seller makes to the buyer, reduces the price unless it buys a distinct good or service from the customer (para. 70). For example (illustration), a subsidiary pays a buyer 100 to build the spur that connects the buyer to its pipeline under a 5,000 gas contract. The spur is the buyer's asset and gives the seller nothing distinct, so revenue over the contract is 4,900."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For provisionally priced sales, the price movement after delivery sits in the receivable (see the Trade receivables essay)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"5. Step 4: allocate the transaction price"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A contract with several obligations needs one price split among them, in proportion to "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"standalone selling prices"},{"type":"text","text":" (SSP), the prices at which each would sell separately. The notes' example sells a turbine, installation and training for 5,000,000, with SSPs of 5,000,000, 100,000 and 50,000:"}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Total SSP = 5,150,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Turbine = 5,000,000 × 5,000,000 / 5,150,000 = 4,854,369"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Installation = 5,000,000 × 100,000 / 5,150,000 = 97,087"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Training = 5,000,000 × 50,000 / 5,150,000 = 48,544"}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"On installation, 1 November 2019: Dr Cash 5,000,000 / Cr Sales revenue 4,854,369 / Cr Service revenue 97,087 / Cr Unearned service revenue (a contract liability) 48,544"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"When an SSP cannot be observed it is estimated by one of three methods (para. 79). The "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"adjusted market assessment"},{"type":"text","text":" starts from what customers in the market, or competitors, charge. "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Expected cost plus a margin"},{"type":"text","text":" builds the price up from cost. The "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"residual approach"},{"type":"text","text":" takes the total price less the observable SSPs of the other items, and is allowed only when the item's price is highly variable or not yet established. The notes place the turbine example under the residual heading, but it is the relative SSP method, since all three prices are observable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For example (illustration), a PHE services subsidiary sells seismic acquisition (SSP 1,800), data processing (SSP 600) and an interpretation licence it has never priced separately, all for 2,700."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Residual: interpretation = 2,700 − 1,800 − 600 = 300"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cost plus margin: expected cost 230 × 1.25 = 287.5; allocated = 2,700 × 287.5 / 2,687.5 = 288.84"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PHE's policy uses the second, estimating an SSP that \"cannot be observed directly\" from \"expected cost plus a margin\" (Note 3p)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"6. Step 5: recognise revenue at a point in time or over time"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Revenue is recognised when, or as, the customer obtains control of the good or service, meaning the ability to direct its use and obtain substantially all of its remaining benefits. An obligation is satisfied "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"over time"},{"type":"text","text":" if any one of three tests holds (para. 35):"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"the customer receives and consumes the benefit as the entity performs, as with a drilling day or a month of monitoring;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"the entity's performance creates or enhances an asset the customer controls as it is built, such as a platform on the customer's site;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"the asset has no alternative use to the entity and the entity has an enforceable right to payment for work done to date."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Otherwise the obligation is satisfied at a "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"point in time"},{"type":"text","text":", judged by indicators such as a present right to payment, legal title, physical possession, the risks and rewards of ownership, and the customer's acceptance (para. 38). The notes' list of indicators ends with \"the company has received the asset\"; the standard means that the "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"customer"},{"type":"text","text":" has accepted it. For crude, control typically passes at the terminal's loading flange. PHE treats goods as generally satisfied at a point in time and services over time (Note 3p)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Measuring progress."},{"type":"text","text":" For over-time obligations the entity picks one method per obligation: "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"output methods"},{"type":"text","text":", such as metres drilled or units delivered, or "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"input methods"},{"type":"text","text":", such as cost incurred against total expected cost (paras. 39–41, B14–B19). The notes work Kieso's bridge contract of 4,500,000 with the cost-to-cost method."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2019"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2020"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2021"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cost to date"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,000,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2,916,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4,050,000"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Estimated total cost"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4,000,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4,050,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4,050,000"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Percent complete"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"25%"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"72%"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"100%"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Revenue to date"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,125,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3,240,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"4,500,000"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Revenue in the year"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,125,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2,115,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,260,000"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Gross profit in the year"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"125,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"199,000"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"126,000"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"When progress cannot yet be measured reasonably but costs are expected to be recovered, revenue equals cost incurred until it can (para. 45). That is the notes' \"cost-recovery (zero-profit) method\", which defers the bridge's whole 450,000 profit to 2021."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Loss contracts."},{"type":"text","text":" The notes' second loss case raises the 2020 estimate of cost to complete to 1,640,250, so the whole contract now loses money."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Total estimated cost = 2,916,000 + 1,640,250 = 4,556,250; percent complete = 2,916,000 / 4,556,250 = 64%"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Revenue in 2020 = 4,500,000 × 64% − 1,125,000 = 1,755,000; cost in 2020 = 1,916,000; loss on work done = 161,000"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Loss on work still to do = 1,640,250 − 4,500,000 × 36% = 20,250"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Loss recognised in 2020 = 161,000 + 20,250 = 181,250 = 125,000 profit already booked + 56,250 total contract loss"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The notes stop at 161,000 and print 66½ percent in the label while computing with 64 percent. Kieso recognises the whole expected loss at once, and under PSAK the 20,250 for the remaining work is an onerous contract provision under PSAK 237 (formerly PSAK 57, IAS 37), since PSAK 115 itself has no loss rule."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"7. Other recognition issues"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Sales with a right of return."},{"type":"text","text":" Revenue excludes products expected to be returned; the seller records a refund liability and an asset for the right to recover the goods (paras. B20–B21). Using the notes' camera example (100 cameras at 100, cost 60, three returns expected):"}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Accounts receivable 10,000 / Cr Sales revenue 9,700 / Cr Refund liability 300"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dr Cost of goods sold 5,820, Dr Right to recover returned goods 180 / Cr Inventory 6,000"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The notes reach the same net sales and cost by booking returns afterwards, against receivables."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Repurchase agreements."},{"type":"text","text":" If the seller must or may buy the asset back at or above the selling price, the customer never gets control, so the deal is a financing (paras. B66–B68). The notes' Morgan sells an asset for 100,000 and must buy it back for 121,000 two years later, so it books a liability of 100,000 and interest of 10,000 and 11,000 at 10 percent, and no revenue."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Bill-and-hold."},{"type":"text","text":" The notes recognise revenue once the goods cannot be sold elsewhere; PSAK 115 requires four conditions: a substantive reason (the customer asked), goods identified as the customer's, goods ready for transfer, and no ability for the seller to use them or send them elsewhere (para. B81)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Principal or agent."},{"type":"text","text":" When another party is involved, the entity asks whether it controls the good before it passes to the customer (paras. B34–B35). A "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"principal"},{"type":"text","text":" reports gross consideration; an "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"agent"},{"type":"text","text":" reports only its fee or commission (para. B36). Since the 2016 clarifications the indicators point to a principal: primary responsibility for fulfilment, inventory risk, and discretion over price. Credit risk and the form of payment no longer count. The notes' consignment example is the classic agent: Best Valve sells 40,000 of the consignor's goods and records only its 4,000 commission."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The same question decides what an upstream contractor reports. For example (illustration), a cargo of 500 kbbl at USD 75 per barrel (37,500) includes 300 kbbl of the contractor's entitlement and 200 kbbl that belong to the state, sold by the contractor with the proceeds passed on."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contractor as principal for its own barrels only: revenue = 300 × 75 = 22,500"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Proceeds of the state's barrels: 200 × 75 = 15,000, a payable to the Government, not revenue"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here the contractor sells the state's barrels as its agent and never controls them. An overlift is different. The contractor takes the state's barrels as its own and owes the state their value, so the sale is revenue and the debt is booked in cost (section 8)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Warranties and options."},{"type":"text","text":" Assurance warranties are provisions; service warranties and material rights are obligations deferred through a contract liability (see the Deferred revenue essay)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"8. How an upstream contractor's revenue is measured"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Under a production sharing contract (PSC) the state owns the hydrocarbons up to the point of delivery (UU 22/2001 art. 6(2)(a)), and the contractor's "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"entitlement"},{"type":"text","text":" is its share of each year's production, set by the contract (Note 2a, Daftar 5/9–5/11, PDF pp. 26–28). The contractor's revenue is what it lifts and sells to customers, priced for crude at the Indonesian Crude Price (ICP) and for gas at each sales contract's price (Note 2a(iv))."}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Lifting, not entitlement."},{"type":"text","text":" For sales from blocks held with partners, PHE recognises crude and gas revenue on \"the actual lifting amount and sold to customers\". Underlifting and overlifting against final entitlements are valued at the annual weighted average crude price or the gas contract price and booked in direct cost of sales, because they \"are not transactions with customers\" (Note 3p, Daftar 5/62–5/63, PDF pp. 79–80). The Due from the Government essay works the imbalance."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"The DMO fee is revenue from the state."},{"type":"text","text":" The domestic market obligation (DMO) makes the contractor supply part of its crude to the domestic market at the weighted average price or another price set in the PSC (Note 2a(v)). PHE shows DMO fees of 429,402 (Note 35)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Cost recovery makes entitlement depend on cost."},{"type":"text","text":" Under a cost recovery PSC the contractor's entitlement includes barrels that repay its recoverable costs. The Due from the Government essay computes an illustrative entitlement of 2,200 kbbl, worth 165,000, from 4,000 kbbl of production at USD 75, first tranche petroleum (FTP) of 20 percent, a contractor share of 25 percent, and recoverable costs of 120,000. Raise recoverable costs by 12,000 (illustration):"}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cost recovery = 1,600 + 12,000 / 75 = 1,760 kbbl"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Equity to be split = 4,000 − 800 FTP − 1,760 = 1,440 kbbl; contractor's share = 1,440 × 25% = 360 kbbl"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Entitlement = 1,760 + 200 FTP share + 360 = 2,320 kbbl, up 120 kbbl; revenue up 120 × 75 = 9,000"}]}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Gross split removes that link."},{"type":"text","text":" Under a gross split PSC the contractor takes a percentage of gross production, which under the 2017 regulation cited in PHE's Note 2b is made of a base split adjusted by variable and progressive components and ministerial discretion, with no cost recovery (Daftar 5/17, PDF p. 34). The 2024 regulation dropped the base split. With an illustrative contractor split of 60 percent, revenue is 4,000 × 60% × 75 = 180,000 whatever the costs, and the extra 12,000 of cost falls entirely on the contractor's profit."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PHE holds both kinds, and its Corridor PSC moves from gross split to cost recovery from 1 January 2025 (Note 2b). It also has operation cooperation contracts (KSO) in which partners recover costs and split the rest with PHE (Note 2g), and a technical service contract for West Qurna-1 in Iraq, where the contractor earns a remuneration fee on production above a baseline plus recovered petroleum costs, a service fee from the Iraqi state (Note 2f, Daftar 5/23–5/24, PDF pp. 40–41)."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"9. Revenue across industries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Telecom bundles."},{"type":"text","text":" A \"free\" handset with a 24-month plan is two obligations. For example (illustration), a customer pays 30 a month for 24 months (720). Standalone, the handset sells for 600 and the plan for 25 a month (600)."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Handset = 720 × 600 / 1,200 = 360, recognised on day one; Dr Contract asset 360 / Cr Revenue, equipment 360"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Service = 360 over 24 months = 15 a month, though 30 is billed; the contract asset unwinds by 15 a month"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Real estate and construction."},{"type":"text","text":" Under PSAK 44 Indonesian developers used percentage of completion for apartments meeting its conditions. Construction contracts usually meet the second over-time test. Under PSAK 115 a pre-sold apartment is recognised over time only if the developer has an enforceable right to payment for work done to date (para. 35(c)); otherwise revenue waits for handover."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Software and licences."},{"type":"text","text":" A licence that gives a "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"right to use"},{"type":"text","text":" the software as it exists when granted is recognised at a point in time. One that gives a "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"right to access"},{"type":"text","text":" intellectual property the licensor keeps changing, typical of software as a service, is recognised over the licence period (paras. B56–B58). A three-year subscription of 1,000 earns 27.78 a month."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Marketplaces and agents."},{"type":"text","text":" An e-commerce platform that never controls the goods reports its commission. On gross merchandise value of 10,000 at an 8 percent commission its revenue is 800."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Banks and Islamic finance."},{"type":"text","text":" Interest income is outside PSAK 115 and follows PSAK 109 (formerly PSAK 71, IFRS 9); a bank's fees for services are within PSAK 115. In a murabahah under PSAK 402 (formerly PSAK 102), the seller's margin is profit on a sale, recognised as the Trade receivables essay describes."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"10. Presentation and analysis: PHE's Note 35"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 115 asks for revenue from contracts with customers apart from other income (para. 113), "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"disaggregation"},{"type":"text","text":" into categories that show how economic factors affect the nature, amount, timing and uncertainty of revenue (para. 114), contract balances and the revenue released from opening contract liabilities (para. 116), and the price allocated to remaining obligations (para. 120), unless the contract lasts a year or less or the entity bills amounts matching performance to date (para. 121)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PHE disaggregates by counterparty and product (Note 35, Daftar 5/148, PDF p. 165)."}]},{"type":"table","content":[{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2024"}]}]},{"type":"tableHeader","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2023"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Related parties and Government: crude oil and gas"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"9,757,007"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"9,799,637"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Adjustment split PSC"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"703,811"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"859,924"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"DMO fees, crude oil"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"429,402"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"448,841"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Energy distribution, logistics, drilling and support services"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"373,847"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"350,430"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Related parties and Government"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"11,264,067"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"11,458,832"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Third parties: crude oil"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,132,087"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,017,555"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Third parties: gas"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,703,084"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1,848,903"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Third parties: services"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"231,102"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"243,094"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Third parties"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"3,066,273"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"3,109,552"}]}]}]},{"type":"tableRow","content":[{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Total revenues"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"14,330,340"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","attrs":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"colwidth":null,"align":null},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"14,568,384"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Crude oil and gas = 9,757,007 + 1,132,087 + 1,703,084 = 12,592,178, or 87.9% of revenue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Related parties and Government = 11,264,067 / 14,330,340 = 78.6%"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PT Kilang Pertamina Internasional = 7,372,296 / 14,330,340 = 51.4%"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 44g lists the related buyers, including feed gas to the DSLNG plant (523,722), and states that sales are \"after deduction by PNBP\" ("},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Penerimaan Negara Bukan Pajak"},{"type":"text","text":", non-tax state revenue) (Daftar 5/186, PDF p. 203), which fits net reporting of the state's share. The segment note gives the second cut: exploration and production 13,902,984 and services 1,296,023 before eliminating 868,667 of intra-group sales, and by geography 13,642,166 in Indonesia and 1,556,841 overseas (Note 46, Daftar 5/220 and 5/222, PDF pp. 237 and 239), 10.2 percent of the 15,199,007 total before elimination."}]},{"type":"blockquote","attrs":{"variant":"quote"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Trade receivables / revenue × 365 = 3,146,868 / 14,330,340 × 365 = 80 days (2023: 2,768,397 / 14,568,384 × 365 = 69 days)"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Collection slowed in 2024. Receipts from customers of 12,661,461 (Daftar 4, PDF p. 17) are 95.9 percent of revenue excluding the 1,133,213 billed to SKK Migas, which is collected through the separate line for receipts from the Government."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 35 leaves three gaps. The related-party crude and gas line is split only indirectly: Note 44g says sales to Pertamina and KPI are crude (about 7.39 million) and the rest gas. \"Adjustment split PSC\", 703,811, is billed to SKK Migas, whose revenue in Note 44g (1,133,213; 2023: 1,308,765) equals the DMO fees plus this line in both years, but PHE does not say what it compensates. And there is no revenue released from the opening deferred revenue of 11,143 (para. 116(b)), an omission immaterial at 0.08 percent of revenue."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11. Related lines"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/deferred-revenue-current","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"deferred-revenue-current"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/deferred-revenue-current","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"deferred-revenue-non-current"},{"type":"text","text":": contract liabilities, take-or-pay, financing on prepayments."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/trade-receivables-net","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"trade-receivables-net"},{"type":"text","text":": unconditional rights to consideration, contract assets, provisional pricing."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/due-from-government","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"due-from-government"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/due-from-government","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"due-to-government-current"},{"type":"text","text":": underlifting, overlifting, DMO fees."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/production-expenses","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"production-expenses"},{"type":"text","text":": the costs PHE recognises \"on the basis of the costs incurred for the actual amount sold\"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/decommissioning-site-restoration-provision","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"decommissioning-site-restoration-provision"},{"type":"text","text":": onerous contract provisions."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"/accounting/fsli/production-expenses","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-primary underline cursor-pointer hover:text-primary/80","title":null}}],"text":"other-income-expense-net"},{"type":"text","text":": gains outside revenue."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Least-confident assertions"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading PHE's \"after deduction by PNBP\" as net reporting of the state's share is an inference. The FS do not say whether PHE ever sells the state's barrels, and the illustration of 200 kbbl of state crude is constructed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"What \"Adjustment split PSC\" (703,811 in 2024, 859,924 in 2023) compensates is not disclosed; its counterparty is SKK Migas (Notes 35, 44g), as the Due from the Government essay also reports. One unverified reading is compensation from the state's share for gas sold at regulated prices to designated industries ("},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"harga gas bumi tertentu"},{"type":"text","text":", HGBT), since Permen ESDM 15/2022 funds that price cut from the state's share and keeps the contractor's share whole. On that reading it is consideration for gas delivered, consistent with Note 3p. A split true-up is the other possibility."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PHE's Note 2b still cites ESDM Regulations 8/2017 and 52/2017 for gross split. Regulation 13/2024 revoked them in August 2024, before the year end, dropped the base split and, per ESDM, puts contractor shares at 75–95 percent (secondary sources); existing contracts may keep their signed terms. The 60 percent split is an illustration."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note 3p's list of five steps is garbled in both languages: \"identify contracts\" is unnumbered, then steps 1 and 2 both read \"identification of performance obligations\". Note 35's PT Kilang Pertamina Internasional figure (7,372,296) differs by 1 from Note 44g (7,372,295). The about 7.39 million of related-party crude is approximate, because the Note 44g rows also carry services."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Treating TSC cost recovery as part of service revenue, and the control point for crude at the loading flange, are general industry readings. PHE does not state either."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"References"}]},{"type":"orderedList","attrs":{"start":1,"type":null},"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PT Pertamina Hulu Energi dan Entitas Anak, consolidated financial statements 31 December 2024 (audited, USD thousand): statement of profit or loss (Daftar 2/1, PDF p. 14); cash flow statement (Daftar 4, PDF p. 17); Note 2a (Daftar 5/9–5/11, PDF pp. 26–28); Note 2b (Daftar 5/17–5/18, PDF pp. 34–35); Note 2f and 2g (Daftar 5/23–5/25, PDF pp. 40–42); Note 3p (Daftar 5/61–5/63, PDF pp. 78–80); Note 35 (Daftar 5/148, PDF p. 165); Note 44g (Daftar 5/186, PDF p. 203); Note 46 (Daftar 5/220–5/222, PDF pp. 237–239). Totals cross-checked to the PHE FS 2024 data extract. VERIFIED (PHE FS 2024, on disk)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lecture notes this series follows, \"Inter 2 – Chapter 18 – Revenue Recognition\" (Rumpun Akuntansi Keuangan): asset-liability approach, five steps (Airbus–Garuda), variable consideration (builder's bonus, 147,500), time value (Pertamina–Shell note), non-cash consideration, consideration payable, allocation (turbine), returns (cameras), repurchase (Morgan), bill-and-hold, principal/agent, consignment, warranties, cost-to-cost and zero-profit methods (bridge), loss contracts, franchises. NOTES. Corrected here: the turbine example is relative SSP, not residual; the last control indicator refers to the customer's acceptance; the loss on the unprofitable contract is 181,250, not 161,000; bill-and-hold needs the four conditions of para. B81; returns are estimated at the sale; the notes' third over-time criterion omits the enforceable right to payment. Minor slips not used here: the interest journal dated 1 December (31 December) and \"revenue recognized in 2019\" in both loss cases (2020)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lecture notes, \"TA – Chapter 9 – Revenue\": the older (PSAK 23) definition of revenue, revenue versus gains, the realised-or-realisable and earned criteria. NOTES."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 115 "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Pendapatan dari Kontrak dengan Pelanggan"},{"type":"text","text":" (IFRS 15). Paras. 9, 22, 25, 27, 35, 38, 39–41, 44–45, 53–57, 65–70, 79, 113–116, 120–121, B14–B21, B34–B36, B56–B58, B66–B68, B79–B81 and Appendix A (customer, revenue) VERIFIED (web, IFRS 15 as adopted, Commission Regulation (EU) 2016/1905, Official Journal L 295, 29.10.2016, via legislation.gov.uk). The 2016 Clarifications recasting B37 as indicators of a principal and removing the credit-risk indicator VERIFIED (web, BDO Australia, May 2016; IAS Plus); the removal of the commission indicator is STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED. Treatment of cash received when the para. 9 criteria fail (para. 15) STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"PSAK 72 effective 1 January 2020, replacing PSAK 23, PSAK 34, PSAK 44 and ISAK 10, 21, 27. VERIFIED (web, secondary: Indonesian journal articles citing IAI). PSAK 115, 237, 109 and 402 numbers VERIFIED (web, IAI renumbering list, as in sibling essays); content of PSAK 237 and 402 STANDARD — NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Peraturan Menteri ESDM No. 13 Tahun 2024 on gross split PSCs, revoking Permen ESDM 8/2017 as amended by 12/2020. VERIFIED (web, BPK peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/296590; ESDM press release, 1 Oct 2024). The enactment date is 6 August 2024 per BPK; one news source gives 12 August. Removal of the base split and the 75–95 percent range VERIFIED (web, secondary: Katadata; ESDM release; Fortune IDN)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"UU No. 22/2001 on Oil and Gas, art. 6(2)(a), state ownership up to the point of delivery. VERIFIED (web, secondary: ESDM, \"Kedaulatan negara dalam pengusahaan migas\"); statute text not opened."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Permen ESDM No. 15/2022 on HGBT: price adjustment deducted from the state's share, contractor's share unaffected. VERIFIED (web, secondary: Ditjen Migas ESDM, \"Pokok-pokok isi Permen ESDM Nomor 15 Tahun 2022\"). Its application to PHE's \"Adjustment split PSC\" NOT VERIFIED."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Kieso, Weygandt and Warfield, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Intermediate Accounting"},{"type":"text","text":", IFRS edition, ch. 18, the textbook the lecture notes summarise (bridge contract and the 181,250 loss). Not on disk; NOT VERIFIED."}]}]}]}]}$j$::jsonb
   where e.id = 'd29a13f3-0f60-4efe-b744-172af36d2d62'
     and e.section = 'accounting'
     and e.content_json is null
     and md5(e.content) = '3aa1306703c422af0c4c04baa2801cde'
  returning e.id, e.title, e.snippet, e.status, e.content_json
), rev as (
  insert into public.essay_revisions (essay_id, revision_no, change_type, title, snippet, content_json, status, change_summary, changed_by)
  select up.id, coalesce((select max(x.revision_no) from public.essay_revisions x where x.essay_id = up.id), 0) + 1, 'migration',
         up.title, up.snippet, up.content_json, up.status,
         'content_json backfilled: the TipTap document the stored content was serialised from (accounting import, 22 Oct 2026). content unchanged.', null
